  ('tx18-green', 'no_corp_pac', 2, 'Accepts some PAC money.', null, true),
  ('tx28-cuellar', 'abortion', 0, 'Was the only House Democrat to vote against the Women''s Health Protection Act in 2021 and 2022; no reproductive rights cosponsorship in the 119th Congress. Opposes codifying Roe.', 'https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/house-bill/3755', false),
  ('tx28-cuellar', 'gnd', 0, 'Cosponsors H.R.662, the Promoting Domestic Energy Production Act, and H.R.8990, the Protect Domestic Oil and Gas Small Business Act of 2026, with no clean energy or climate bill on his 119th Congress record. Actively promotes oil and gas expansion.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/henry-cuellar/C001063', false),
  ('tx28-cuellar', 'immigration', 1, 'Cosponsors H.R.5260, the Pay Our Border Patrol and Customs Agents Act, H.R.389, the Southern Border Farmers and Ranchers Protection Act, and a resolution honouring the retiring Border Patrol chief, alongside H.R.1589, the American Dream and Promise Act. Border-security-first with a Dreamer measure; backed Title 42 extension.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/henry-cuellar/C001063', true),
  ('tx28-cuellar', 'labor', 1, 'Cosponsors H.R.2692, the No Tax Breaks for Union Busting Act, and H.R.2671, the Tax Fairness for Workers Act, but not H.R.20, the PRO Act, which he has opposed in part. Selective labor support.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/henry-cuellar/C001063', false),
  ('tx28-cuellar', 'no_corp_pac', 0, 'Heavy corporate PAC funding throughout his career; indicted in May 2024 on bribery and money laundering charges involving Azerbaijan and a Mexican bank; AIPAC-aligned money has supported him. Takes corporate PAC money and benefits from AIPAC-linked spending.', 'https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/congressman-and-his-wife-charged-bribery-unlawful-foreign-influence-and-money-laundering', false),
  ('tx34-gonzalez', 'gnd', 1, 'Cosponsors H.R.662, the Promoting Domestic Energy Production Act, H.R.8990, the Protect Domestic Oil and Gas Small Business Act, H.R.3699, the Energy Choice Act, and a resolution celebrating LNG exports. Nothing on clean energy or climate. Held at 1 rather than 0 only because he has not cosponsored rollback of existing climate law; arguably a 0 like Cuellar.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/vicente-gonzalez/G000581', true),
  ('tx34-gonzalez', 'immigration', 1, 'Voted for the Laken Riley Act (S.5) on January 22, 2025, Roll no. 23, mandating detention of undocumented immigrants accused of theft; cosponsors the Border Airport Fairness Act and H.R.1589, the American Dream and Promise Act. Enforcement-first with a Dreamer measure.', 'https://clerk.house.gov/Votes/202523', false),
  ('tx34-gonzalez', 'm4a', 1, 'Cosponsors H.R.2045, the Medicare Dental, Vision, and Hearing Benefit Act, and H.R.5145 extending premium tax credits; opposes single payer. Incremental Medicare expansion within the existing system.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/vicente-gonzalez/G000581', true),
  ('tx34-gonzalez', 'no_corp_pac', 1, 'Accepts corporate PAC money; no pledge.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/vicente-gonzalez/G000581', true),
  ('tx37-casar', 'antitrust', 3, 'Cosponsors H.R.4528, the Price Gouging Prevention Act, H.R.4966 on grocery price gouging, H.R.9875, the Protecting Childcare from Private Equity Act, and H.R.5106, the Restore Trust in Congress Act stock ban. Price gouging enforcement, private equity limits and a stock ban; breakups of Big Tech not found by name.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/greg-casar/C001131', false),
  ('tx37-casar', 'gaza', 4, 'Cosponsors H.R.3565, the Block the Bombs Act, limiting offensive weapons transfers to Israel; original cosponsor listed at introduction in June 2025. Cosponsors a bill blocking offensive arms transfers.', 'https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/3565/cosponsors', false),
  ('tx37-casar', 'gnd', 4, 'Cosponsors H.R.10063, the Green New Deal for Public Housing Act, and H.R.4714, the End Polluter Welfare Act of 2025, which eliminates fossil fuel subsidies. Green New Deal cosponsor plus ending subsidies.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/greg-casar/C001131', false),
  ('tx37-casar', 'housing', 4, 'Cosponsors H.R.4457, the Housing Is a Human Right Act, H.R.3049, the Tenants'' Right to Organize Act, H.R.6124, the End Rent Fixing Act, H.R.4100 ending junk fees for renters, and H.R.10063, the Green New Deal for Public Housing Act. Social housing investment plus tenant protections.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/greg-casar/C001131', false),
  ('tx37-casar', 'immigration', 4, 'Cosponsors H.R.6397, the Dignity for Detained Immigrants Act ending private detention contracts, H.R.1589, the American Dream and Promise Act, H.R.4456, the Stop ICE from Kidnapping U.S. Citizens Act, and H.R.10040, the No TSA Data for ICE Act. Pathway plus ending detention contracts.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/greg-casar/C001131', false),
  ('tx37-casar', 'justice', 4, 'Cosponsors H.R.5361, the George Floyd Justice in Policing Act of 2025; as an Austin council member led the 2020 police budget reallocation. George Floyd Act plus a reallocation record.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/greg-casar/C001131', false),
  ('tx37-casar', 'labor', 4, 'Cosponsors H.R.20, the PRO Act, H.R.4443, the Asuncion Valdivia Heat Illness Prevention Act, and H.R.4693, the College Athlete Right to Organize Act; staged a thirst strike in 2023 for a federal heat standard. Former Workers Defense Project organizer. PRO Act plus a union-led record.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/greg-casar/C001131', false),
  ('tx37-casar', 'm4a', 4, 'Original cosponsor of H.R.3069, the Medicare for All Act (2025-04-29).', 'https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/3069/cosponsors', false),
  ('tx37-casar', 'no_corp_pac', 4, 'FEC itemized receipts: of $827K in non-individual receipts, $526K is ActBlue conduit, i.e. small-dollar individual money, and $23K is his own victory fund. Actual PAC money is mostly labor (SEIU, AFSCME, IBEW, UAW, Machinists) plus JStreetPAC, Demand Justice and Jane Fonda Climate PAC. One exception: $5,000 from the National Beer Wholesalers Association PAC, a corporate trade association, which sits awkwardly with a level 4 no-corporate-PAC score.', 'https://www.fec.gov/data/receipts/?committee_id=C00791897&two_year_transaction_period=2026', false),
  ('tx37-casar', 'tax', 4, 'Cosponsor of H.R.8085, the Ultra-Millionaire Tax Act of 2026 as of 2026-03-26.', 'https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/8085/cosponsors', false),
  ('ut01-mcadams', 'antitrust', 2, 'Cosponsored the Ban Conflicted Trading Act as a congressman in 2019. Stock ban.', 'https://www.congress.gov/bill/116th-congress/house-bill/1081/cosponsors', false),
  ('ut01-mcadams', 'm4a', 1, 'Blue Dog who opposed Medicare for All in Congress; favours ACA reforms. Incremental.', 'https://www.predictionedge.com/elections/profile/ben-mcadams/', true),
  ('ut01-mcadams', 'no_corp_pac', 1, 'Accepts corporate PAC money; no pledge. FEC: 8.5% of receipts from other political committees (includes ActBlue conduit).', 'https://api.open.fec.gov', true),
  ('wi03-cooke', 'abortion', 3, 'Campaign site: codify Roe and repeal the Hyde Amendment. Both named.', 'https://www.rebeccaforcongress.com/', true),
  ('wi03-cooke', 'labor', 3, 'Endorsed by the Wisconsin AFL-CIO and building trades; campaign site supports the PRO Act. PRO Act by name per site; not retrieved verbatim this pass.', 'https://www.rebeccaforcongress.com/', true),
  ('wi03-cooke', 'm4a', 2, 'Campaign: public option and rural hospital access; not single payer.', 'https://www.rebeccaforcongress.com/', true),
  ('wi03-cooke', 'no_corp_pac', 3, 'Campaign pledges no corporate PAC money. FEC: 6.1% of receipts from other political committees (includes ActBlue conduit).', 'https://api.open.fec.gov', true),
  ('sen-tx-talarico', 'abortion', 2, 'BallotReady platform: "Codify Roe v. Wade and protect access to contraception and IVF." Voted against Texas''s abortion ban without exceptions. Lowered from 3 to 2: codify Roe; no Hyde repeal named.', 'https://www.ballotready.org/people/james-talarico', false),
  ('sen-tx-talarico', 'democracy', 3, 'Broke quorum in 2021 over the Texas voting bill and in 2025 over mid-decade redistricting; campaign site names getting billionaire mega-donors and dark money out of politics. Voting rights and money in politics; no filibuster or Court position retrieved.', 'https://www.votetalarico.org/', true),
  ('sen-tx-talarico', 'gaza', 4, 'San Antonio Current, January 2026 New Braunfels town hall: told the crowd he will work to ban the sale of offensive military weapons to Israel if elected, saying Netanyahu "does not have the right to use famine or collective punishment"; has disavowed AIPAC and pledged not to take its support. Raised from 2 to 4: campaigns on blocking offensive arms transfers and refuses AIPAC. Provisional because he declined in September 2025 to say how he would have voted on the Sanders resolutions and does not use the word genocide.', 'https://www.sacurrent.com/news/politics-and-elections/talarico-says-he-will-ban-sale-of-offensive-weapons-to-israel/', true),
  ('sen-tx-talarico', 'labor', 2, 'BallotReady platform: raise the federal minimum wage to $15 an hour and tax corporations with extreme CEO-to-worker pay ratios. Lowered from 3 to 2: $15 is below the $17 threshold and the PRO Act is not named on his platform.', 'https://www.ballotready.org/people/james-talarico', false),
  ('sen-tx-talarico', 'm4a', 2, 'Smarter.vote: supports a Medicare public option, "Medicare for Y''all," letting any American buy into Medicare, rather than single-payer Medicare for All; protect and improve the ACA; capped insulin copays at $25 in Texas. Lowered from 3 to 2: public option, not single payer.', 'https://smarter.vote/', false),
  ('sen-tx-talarico', 'no_corp_pac', 4, 'Campaign site: running against billionaire mega-donors and dark money; told wealthy supporters they are welcome only if they accept being taxed more and having their political influence limited. Refuses corporate PAC money; $8.7M in outside spending supported him.', 'https://www.votetalarico.org/', true),
  ('sen-tx-talarico', 'tax', 3, 'BallotReady platform: "Make billionaires pay their fair share in taxes, including by imposing a higher tax on their income and capital gains and ending the dubious buy, borrow, die loopholes," raise the corporate tax rate, and a special tax on corporations paying CEOs more than 250 times the median worker. Higher corporate rate plus capital gains reform; no wealth tax by name.', 'https://www.ballotready.org/people/james-talarico', false),
  ('sen-tx-crockett', 'democracy', 3, 'Quorum-break veteran; voting rights focus.', null, true),
  ('sen-tx-crockett', 'gaza', 3, 'Voted to block some offensive arms sales.', null, true),
  ('sen-tx-crockett', 'justice', 3, 'Original cosponsor of H.R.5361, the George Floyd Justice in Policing Act of 2025 (2025-09-15).', 'https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/5361/cosponsors', false),
  ('sen-tx-crockett', 'm4a', 4, 'Original cosponsor of H.R.3069, the Medicare for All Act (2025-04-29).', 'https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/3069/cosponsors', false),
  ('sen-tx-crockett', 'no_corp_pac', 2, 'Accepts some PAC money.', null, true),
  ('sen-mi-el-sayed', 'gaza', 4, 'Campaign hotline ad, his own voice: "I oppose direct foreign military funding," listing Israel alongside Vietnam and Iraq as cases where America broke its own rules; his campaign touts that 60% of Michigan voters oppose increasing military aid to Israel. AIPAC''s United Democracy Project spent $22.5M against him. Opposes military aid; refuses and is targeted by AIPAC.', 'https://abdulforsenate.com/2026/07/new-ad-1-844-abdul-4-u/', false),
  ('sen-mi-el-sayed', 'gnd', 4, 'Priorities page commits to clean air and water; supports a Green New Deal per his 2018 gubernatorial platform. No 2026 statement on fossil fuel phaseout or public power retrieved; score retained from prior file, provisional.', 'https://abdulforsenate.com/priorities/', true),
  ('sen-mi-el-sayed', 'immigration', 4, 'Final debate, his own words: "I''m going to say that I think we need to abolish ICE because I am not afraid of what they''re going to say about me." Raised from 3 to 4: abolish ICE by name.', 'https://abdulforsenate.com/2026/07/new-at-final-debate-dr-abdul-el-sayed-proves-hes-ready-for-november/', false),
  ('sen-mi-el-sayed', 'labor', 3, 'Hotline ad: "I oppose corporate tax breaks, support unions, fair wages, and Medicare for all... which of course is why the UAW has supported me." UAW endorsement; the PRO Act is not named in the retrieved material.', 'https://abdulforsenate.com/2026/07/new-ad-1-844-abdul-4-u/', true),
  ('sen-mi-el-sayed', 'm4a', 4, 'Campaign priorities page: his three stated priorities are "get money out of politics, put money in your pocket, and pass Medicare for All." Named directly and central.', 'https://abdulforsenate.com/priorities/', false),
  ('sen-mi-el-sayed', 'no_corp_pac', 4, 'Priorities: get money out of politics; attacked Stevens for a $60 million super PAC "crutch" and SpaceX PAC money, and campaigns on refusing corporate PAC money. Refuses corporate PAC money and disavows super PAC spending on his own behalf.', 'https://abdulforsenate.com/2026/07/new-at-final-debate-dr-abdul-el-sayed-proves-hes-ready-for-november/', false),
  ('sen-mi-el-sayed', 'tax', 4, 'First debate: "How about we start taxing billionaires their wealth, so that we can return trillions of dollars to the economy?" Final debate: "We have the opportunity to tax billionaires their wealth." Wealth tax on billionaires by name.', 'https://abdulforsenate.com/2026/07/dr-abdul-el-sayed-cements-frontrunner-status-in-first-head-to-head-u-s-senate-debate/', false),
