  ('sen-me-jackson', 'antitrust', 3, 'Advocated a legally binding moratorium on private equity purchases of independent health care practices in Maine and campaigns on stopping Wall Street from buying up Maine homes. Private equity regulation; no stock trading ban or Big Tech position retrieved.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Troy_Jackson', true),
  ('sen-me-jackson', 'labor', 4, 'Fifth-generation logger who led a 1998 logging blockade; as Senate President passed Maine''s pro-labor agenda; endorsed by the Maine AFL-CIO. Union-led campaign with a governing record; the PRO Act is not named in retrieved material but his record is the strongest labor record in the file.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Troy_Jackson', true),
  ('sen-me-jackson', 'm4a', 3, 'Prediction Edge: "expresses support for Medicare for All in principle but views a public option as the practical path for Maine." Wikipedia summary: supports Medicare for All. Supports single payer in principle while proposing a public option; 3 holds.', 'https://www.predictionedge.com/elections/profile/troy-jackson/', true),
  ('sen-me-jackson', 'no_corp_pac', 4, 'His own post on X, quoted by JTA: "rejecting all money from corporate PACs, AIPAC, and lobbyists from Big Oil and Big Pharma." Campaign site: not backed by corporate PACs or billionaire donors. No corporate PAC, no lobbyist money, refuses AIPAC. $3.1M in outside spending supported him.', 'https://www.jta.org/2026/07/24/politics/maine-democratic-senate-nominee-in-waiting-troy-jackson-raises-eyebrows-in-the-jewish-community', false),
  ('sen-me-jackson', 'tax', 3, 'Maine Public: pays for his plan through "a fair tax system," voted against the 2011 tax cuts for the wealthy in defiance of his own leadership; Prediction Edge: exploring surcharges on luxury homes and raising taxes on the wealthy. Higher taxes on the wealthy without a wealth tax by name.', 'https://www.mainepublic.org/politics/2026-04-17/your-vote-2026-profile-troy-jackson-democrat-for-governor', true),
