  ('sen-nc-cooper', 'abortion', 3, 'Ballotpedia: vetoed the 12-week ban in 2023, which the legislature overrode. Vetoed a restriction; no federal codification or Hyde commitment retrieved, so the 3 rests on the veto record.', 'https://ballotpedia.org/Roy_Cooper', true),
  ('sen-nc-cooper', 'gnd', 2, 'As governor issued clean energy and offshore wind executive orders while supporting natural gas expansion. IRA-style incentives without a fossil phaseout.', 'https://ballotpedia.org/Roy_Cooper', true),
  ('sen-nc-cooper', 'labor', 2, 'Battleground Vote: raised teacher pay and state employee wages; North Carolina remains a right-to-work state and no PRO Act or wage-floor commitment retrieved.', 'https://battlegroundvote.com/north-carolina/roy-cooper', true),
  ('sen-nc-cooper', 'm4a', 2, 'Battleground Vote and Ballotpedia: signed Medicaid expansion in March 2023 covering more than 600,000 North Carolinians; his Senate campaign runs a "Make Stuff Cost Less" tour centred on health costs and Medicaid. Coverage expansion within the existing system; no public option or single payer commitment retrieved. Held at 2 on the strength of the expansion record.', 'https://battlegroundvote.com/north-carolina/roy-cooper', true),
  ('sen-nc-cooper', 'no_corp_pac', 1, 'Accepts corporate PAC money; Senate Majority PAC committed $11M for the fall and $18M was spent against him. No pledge.', 'https://nsjonline.com/article/2026/08/cooper-joint-fundraising-with-progressive-senators-tops-726k/', true),
  ('sen-ga-ossoff', 'antitrust', 3, 'Sponsored the Ban Congressional Stock Trading Act in the 118th Congress and cosponsors S.1879 in the 119th. Stock ban; breakups not named.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/jon-ossoff/O000174', false),
  ('sen-ga-ossoff', 'democracy', 3, 'Cosponsors S.2523, the John R. Lewis Voting Rights Advancement Act; voted to change Senate rules for voting rights legislation in January 2022. Voting rights plus a filibuster-carveout vote; no Citizens United amendment or Court term limits.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/jon-ossoff/O000174', true),
  ('sen-ga-ossoff', 'gaza', 3, 'Voted Yea on November 20, 2024 to discharge S.J.Res.111 blocking a $774 million tank round sale to Israel (rejected 18-79), then Nay on July 30, 2025 on S.J.Res.34 blocking a $675.7 million sale (rejected 24-73). Raised from 2 to 3: has voted to block an offensive arms transfer once, and supports conditioning; not 4 because he voted against the 2025 resolution.', 'https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1182/vote_118_2_00292.xml', true),
  ('sen-ga-ossoff', 'm4a', 2, 'Supports a public option and Medicaid expansion; not single payer.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/jon-ossoff/O000174', true),
  ('sen-ga-ossoff', 'no_corp_pac', 3, 'Has refused corporate PAC money since 2020. $5.3M in outside spending supported him.', 'https://www.electjon.com/', true),
  ('sen-oh-brown', 'antitrust', 4, 'As Banking Committee chair, blocked crypto-friendly legislation and pressed enforcement against Wall Street and private equity, which is why Fairshake spent to defeat him in 2024. Breakups plus private equity and crypto regulation record.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/sherrod-brown/B000944', true),
  ('sen-oh-brown', 'gaza', 1, 'Voted Nay on November 20, 2024 on the motion to discharge S.J.Res.111, which would have blocked a $774 million sale of 120mm tank rounds to Israel (rejected 18-79), in his final weeks in the Senate. No ceasefire or arms-conditioning measure on his record. Score of 1 retained; the vote confirms opposition to blocking arms transfers.', 'https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1182/vote_118_2_00292.xml', false),
  ('sen-oh-brown', 'labor', 4, 'Lead Senate sponsor of the PRO Act in the 117th and 118th Congresses; two decades as the Senate''s labor populist, from the auto rescue to the Butch Lewis pension fix. PRO Act sponsor with a union-led record.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/sherrod-brown/B000944', false),
  ('sen-oh-brown', 'm4a', 2, 'Sponsored Medicare at 50 legislation and backs a public option; has not endorsed single payer. Public option, not single payer.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/sherrod-brown/B000944', true),
  ('sen-oh-brown', 'no_corp_pac', 2, 'Accepts some PAC money while running a small-dollar heavy operation; no corporate PAC pledge. $7.6M in outside spending supported him.', 'https://guides.vote/guide/2026-ohio-senate-voters-guide/', true),
  ('sen-oh-brown', 'tax', 3, 'Proposed the Patriot Corporation Act and a worker dividend, and backed corporate rate increases; Guides.vote: supports raising taxes on the wealthy and corporations. Higher corporate rate plus reform; no wealth tax by name.', 'https://guides.vote/guide/2026-ohio-senate-voters-guide/', true),
