  ('sen-me-collins', 'gaza', 0, 'Voted Nay on the motion to discharge S.J.Res.34, which would have blocked a $675.7 million offensive arms sale to Israel, July 30, 2025. Coded from the arms-transfer clause of level 0; the AIPAC-backing clause was not separately verified.', 'https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1191/vote_119_1_00455.htm', true),
  ('sen-ne-ricketts', 'gaza', 0, 'Voted Nay on the motion to discharge S.J.Res.34, which would have blocked a $675.7 million offensive arms sale to Israel, July 30, 2025. Coded from the arms-transfer clause of level 0; the AIPAC-backing clause was not separately verified.', 'https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1191/vote_119_1_00455.htm', true),
  ('sen-oh-husted', 'gaza', 0, 'Voted Nay on the motion to discharge S.J.Res.34, which would have blocked a $675.7 million offensive arms sale to Israel, July 30, 2025. Coded from the arms-transfer clause of level 0; the AIPAC-backing clause was not separately verified.', 'https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1191/vote_119_1_00455.htm', true),
  ('mi07-lawrence', 'm4a', 4, 'Platform: "I support Medicare for All, which would remove the profit motive from health insurance." Named directly.', 'https://wewill2026.com/platform/', true),
  ('mi07-lawrence', 'gnd', 3, 'Platform commits to climate investment, adaptation and taking on Big Utilities, and he co-founded the Sunrise Movement, but the site does not name the Green New Deal or commit to ending fossil subsidies and new leasing. Coded 3 rather than 4 on the site text.', 'https://wewill2026.com/platform/', true),
  ('mi07-lawrence', 'labor', 3, 'Platform: "I support the Protecting the Right to Organize (PRO) Act" and "I have walked on the picket line with GM and Starbucks workers in the 7th District." No sectoral bargaining or $17 wage commitment, so not 4.', 'https://wewill2026.com/platform/', true),
  ('mi07-lawrence', 'no_corp_pac', 3, 'Platform and homepage: "independent of DC insiders and unbought by corporate money," small-dollar ActBlue fundraising. No explicit disavowal of outside super PAC spending, so not 4.', 'https://wewill2026.com/platform/', true),
  ('mi07-lawrence', 'gaza', 4, 'Platform: "we must stop arming Israel, which is pursuing a genocide of Palestinians in Gaza with U.S. weapons and tax dollars," and homepage priority "Stop arms sales to Israel and other human rights violators."', 'https://wewill2026.com/platform/', true),
  ('mi07-lawrence', 'housing', 3, 'Platform backs major federal housing investment, a federal tenant bill of rights, Housing First and ending corporate landlord price-gouging. No rent stabilization or tenant right to counsel by name, so not 4.', 'https://wewill2026.com/platform/', true),
  ('mi07-lawrence', 'tax', 4, 'Platform: "I support a billionaire minimum tax, which is a minimum wealth tax rate that the mega-wealthy must pay." Named directly.', 'https://wewill2026.com/platform/', true),
  ('mi07-lawrence', 'abortion', 2, 'Platform: "I will defend women’s right to choose an abortion, and seek to codify this right in federal law." No Hyde repeal, so 2.', 'https://wewill2026.com/platform/', true),
  ('mi07-lawrence', 'immigration', 3, 'Platform: "I support a path to citizenship for undocumented immigrants" and "End the ICE occupation of American cities." Stops short of defunding or abolishing ICE enforcement and ending detention contracts, so 3.', 'https://wewill2026.com/platform/', true),
  ('mi07-lawrence', 'antitrust', 2, 'Platform backs banning stock trading by members of Congress and questions Big Tech power, but does not call for breakups or private equity regulation.', 'https://wewill2026.com/platform/', true),
  ('pa07-brooks', 'm4a', 4, 'Platform: "Because of this, I support Medicare for All." Named directly.', 'https://brooksforcongress.com/issues/', true),
  ('pa07-brooks', 'gnd', 2, 'Platform backs clean energy jobs, wind and solar, but also commits to approving "new nuclear and natural gas power plants." No fossil fuel phaseout, so 2.', 'https://brooksforcongress.com/issues/', true),
  ('pa07-brooks', 'labor', 3, 'Platform: "I will make it easier to join a union by passing the PRO Act." Union president of the Pennsylvania Professional Fire Fighters Association. No sectoral bargaining or $17 wage figure, so not 4.', 'https://brooksforcongress.com/issues/', true),
  ('pa07-brooks', 'no_corp_pac', 3, 'FEC itemized receipts: of $1.53M in non-individual receipts, $727K is ActBlue and a further $272K is other conduits (Oath.vote, Democracy Engine, Swing Left, GiveGreen), all small-dollar pass-through. Remaining PAC money is union (CWA, Ironworkers, Carpenters, Machinists) plus LCV Action Fund, JStreetPAC and Medicare for All PAC. No corporate PAC receipts found, so the level 3 score holds.', 'https://www.fec.gov/data/receipts/?committee_id=C00917096&two_year_transaction_period=2026', false),
  ('pa07-brooks', 'housing', 2, 'Platform: build more starter homes, increase market-rate housing, crack down on corporate landlords and private equity purchases, cut permitting red tape, pass the HELPER Act. Supply and homebuyer focused rather than tenant protections and public investment.', 'https://brooksforcongress.com/issues/', true),
  ('pa07-brooks', 'tax', 4, 'Platform: "We need to pass a billionaire minimum tax: a baseline tax rate the ultra-wealthy can’t dodge." Named directly.', 'https://brooksforcongress.com/issues/', true),
  ('pa07-brooks', 'abortion', 2, 'Platform: "We need to codify Roe v. Wade" and pass legislation overturning state abortion bans. No Hyde repeal, so 2.', 'https://brooksforcongress.com/issues/', true),
  ('pa07-brooks', 'immigration', 1, 'Platform section is titled "Secure the border and build a working immigration system" and leads with deterring illegal entry, while also backing earned citizenship for law-abiding immigrants and condemning masked ICE arrests. Border-security-first framing.', 'https://brooksforcongress.com/issues/', true),
  ('pa07-brooks', 'justice', 1, 'Platform focuses on resourcing first responders, community trust and investment in mental health and addiction services. No qualified immunity, decarceration or George Floyd Act position.', 'https://brooksforcongress.com/issues/', true),
  ('pa07-brooks', 'antitrust', 2, 'Platform: "No stock trading in Congress" plus generic "antitrust action" and price-gouging enforcement. No Big Tech breakup or private equity regulation commitment.', 'https://brooksforcongress.com/issues/', true),
  ('pa07-brooks', 'democracy', 2, 'Platform: "pass a constitutional amendment to overturn Citizens United," term limits and a congressional stock trading ban. No position on the filibuster or Supreme Court reform.', 'https://brooksforcongress.com/issues/', true),
  ('me02-dunlap', 'm4a', 4, 'Maine Morning Star voter guide: Dunlap "supports a Medicare-for-All system, and putting people’s health and financial well-being over private profits for insurance companies." Named directly.', 'https://mainemorningstar.com/voter-guides/contests/2026-democratic-primary-u-s-house-district-2/', true),
  ('me02-dunlap', 'tax', 4, 'Maine Morning Star voter guide: Dunlap "supports the billionaire tax proposed by U.S. Sen. Bernie Sanders and U.S. Rep. Ro Khanna." Billionaire tax by name.', 'https://mainemorningstar.com/voter-guides/contests/2026-democratic-primary-u-s-house-district-2/', true),
  ('me02-dunlap', 'housing', 2, 'Maine Morning Star voter guide: removing barriers to construction, cutting red tape and investing to boost supply, plus taking on Wall Street and private equity homebuyers. Supply focused, no tenant protections or public housing commitment.', 'https://mainemorningstar.com/voter-guides/contests/2026-democratic-primary-u-s-house-district-2/', true),
  ('me02-dunlap', 'gnd', 2, 'Maine Morning Star voter guide: short-term relief on heating oil prices, long-term investment in domestically produced renewables. No fossil fuel phaseout or Green New Deal language.', 'https://mainemorningstar.com/voter-guides/contests/2026-democratic-primary-u-s-house-district-2/', true),
  ('me02-dunlap', 'immigration', 2, 'Maine Morning Star voter guide: calls recent ICE conduct indiscriminate and heavy-handed and would cut off supplemental ICE funding and impose oversight, while backing "a secure and orderly border." No explicit pathway to citizenship stated, so not 3.', 'https://mainemorningstar.com/voter-guides/contests/2026-democratic-primary-u-s-house-district-2/', true),
  ('pa08-cognetti', 'no_corp_pac', 2, 'Spotlight PA, July 2026: Cognetti says she will reject corporate PAC money, but has taken $5,000 from Sen. Coons’ leadership PAC and $4,000 from Rep. Katherine Clark’s committee, both heavily funded by corporate PACs. Matches level 2, a pledge alongside indirect PAC support.', 'https://www.spotlightpa.org/news/2026/07/pennsylvania-cognetti-corporate-pac-money-campaign-finance-federal-government/', true),
  ('pa08-cognetti', 'antitrust', 2, 'Campaign message summarized by the Pike County Democratic Committee: ban congressional stock trading, take on monopolies and junk fees including credit card fees. Stock trading ban is level 2; no Big Tech breakup or private equity regulation commitment.', 'https://pikecountydemocrats.org/paige-cognetti-for-congress/', true),
  ('ca11-chan', 'm4a', 4, 'Candidate comparison: Chan "supports Medicare for All which guarantees that every American has a right to health care" and "will work to enact this critical legislation when elected." Named directly.', 'https://www.localcandidates.org/elections/2026-us-house-of-representatives-ca-11/compare/connie-chan-vs-scott-wiener', true),
  ('ca11-chan', 'housing', 3, 'Campaign issues page: federal grants and low-interest loans for low- and middle-income housing, expanded housing tax credits, increased rental assistance, and "support innovative social housing programs"; "relying on corporate developers to build affordable housing hasn''t worked - we need direct federal investments in housing." Social housing and public investment named; no rent stabilization or right to counsel, so 3.', 'https://www.conniechansf.com/issues/issue-2', false),
  ('gov-az-hobbs', 'abortion', 2, 'Arizona Ballot Guide: "Abortion is a very personal decision that belongs between a woman and her doctor. Will veto any legislation that attacks Roe v. Wade." Protects the Roe standard; no Hyde repeal position, so 2.', 'https://arizonaballotguide.com/candidates/katie-hobbs', true),
  ('gov-az-hobbs', 'housing', 2, 'Arizona Ballot Guide: repealed the tax on rent, funded down payment help for first-time homebuyers, and cut permitting red tape. Supply and affordability focused rather than tenant protections or public investment.', 'https://arizonaballotguide.com/candidates/katie-hobbs', true),
  ('gov-az-hobbs', 'tax', 1, 'Championed middle-class tax cuts, a $6,000 senior deduction and eliminating taxes on tips and overtime, and vetoed the 2026 Republican budget arguing it gave breaks to billionaires, data centers and special interests while cutting healthcare and food assistance. Opposition to breaks for the wealthy without any proposal to raise top rates.', 'https://arizonaballotguide.com/candidates/katie-hobbs', true),
  ('gov-az-hobbs', 'immigration', 1, 'Arizona Ballot Guide: has funded scholarships regardless of immigration status while emphasizing fixing a broken system and state border security investments. Border-security-inclusive framing with no stated pathway to citizenship.', 'https://arizonaballotguide.com/candidates/katie-hobbs', true),
  ('ca22-villegas', 'gaza', 3, 'Signed a public ceasefire letter in January 2024, campaigns in solidarity with Palestinians against the war in Gaza, refuses corporate PAC money and is endorsed by Track AIPAC and A New Policy. Raised from 2 to 3: level 2 requires opposing conditions on aid, which does not describe him. Level 4 withheld because neither his site nor his public statements commit to blocking specific arms transfers.', 'https://platform.anewpolicypac.org/candidates/randy-villegas-ca', true),
  ('co08-rutinel', 'gaza', 2, 'Colorado Sun, June 2026: Rutinel had previously called Israel’s conduct in Gaza a genocide, but told the Sun he would continue military funding for Israel while promoting "stability and deescalation." Supports de-escalation while opposing conditions on aid.', 'https://coloradosun.com/2026/06/04/manny-rutinel-changed-positions-healthcare-student-debt-fracking/', true),
  ('co08-rutinel', 'tax', 2, 'Ballotpedia and campaign materials: expand tax credits for working parents, "make billionaires pay what they owe," close corporate loopholes, and opposition to the 2025 reconciliation bill’s tax breaks for the wealthy. No wealth tax or billionaire minimum tax by name.', 'https://coloradosun.com/2026/05/28/manny-rutinel-shannon-bird-colorado-primary-issue-guide/', true),
  ('co08-rutinel', 'housing', 2, 'Colorado Sun candidate guide: Rutinel "would streamline the housing permitting processes." Supply focused, no tenant protections or public investment commitment.', 'https://coloradosun.com/2026/05/28/manny-rutinel-shannon-bird-colorado-primary-issue-guide/', true),
  ('co08-rutinel', 'abortion', 2, 'Described as a steadfast opponent of abortion restrictions and endorsed by reproductive rights organizations. Supports the Roe standard; no Hyde repeal position found.', 'https://www.predictionedge.com/elections/profile/manny-rutinel/', true),
  ('gov-me-pingree', 'housing', 3, 'Maine Morning Star: will invest $100 million a year in developing and preserving affordable homes, take on out-of-state corporations and private equity firms driving up rents, reduce evictions and expand permanent housing for the most vulnerable. Public investment plus tenant-side protections.', 'https://mainemorningstar.com/voter-guides/contests/2026-gubernatorial-democratic-primary/', true),
  ('gov-me-pingree', 'tax', 2, 'Maine Morning Star: supports a more progressive state tax code including a new tax on millionaires, an increased Homestead Exemption, and making seasonal and second-home owners pay more. A top-rate increase rather than a wealth tax.', 'https://mainemorningstar.com/voter-guides/contests/2026-gubernatorial-democratic-primary/', true),
  ('gov-me-pingree', 'immigration', 2, 'Maine Morning Star: will ensure the state does not collaborate with federal immigration enforcement, protect churches, schools, hospitals and courthouses as safe spaces, and require agents to unmask and identify themselves. State-office scope, no federal pathway position.', 'https://mainemorningstar.com/voter-guides/contests/2026-gubernatorial-democratic-primary/', true),
  ('gov-me-bellows', 'housing', 3, 'Maine Morning Star: expand the state housing fund for construction and rehabilitation, invest in eviction prevention, and help renters who cannot afford security deposits and first and last month’s rent. Public investment plus tenant protections.', 'https://mainemorningstar.com/voter-guides/contests/2026-gubernatorial-democratic-primary/', true),
  ('gov-me-bellows', 'gnd', 2, 'Maine Morning Star: cap utility rate of return at 6%, streamline permitting and procurement for clean energy, and install solar for LIHEAP-eligible homes. Clean energy incentives without a fossil fuel phaseout.', 'https://mainemorningstar.com/voter-guides/contests/2026-gubernatorial-democratic-primary/', true),
  ('gov-me-bellows', 'tax', 2, 'Maine Morning Star: an "Economic New Deal" freezing property taxes for residents, funded by higher taxes on non-residents and a 4% millionaires tax raising more than $200 million a year. Top-rate increase rather than a wealth tax.', 'https://mainemorningstar.com/voter-guides/contests/2026-gubernatorial-democratic-primary/', true),
  ('sen-me-jackson', 'housing', 2, 'Maine Morning Star gubernatorial guide: accelerate construction of new housing, bar private equity from buying mobile home parks, assist owners and renters with repairs, and create a statewide housing appeals board to cut red tape. Supply and anti-private-equity focused.', 'https://mainemorningstar.com/voter-guides/contests/2026-gubernatorial-democratic-primary/', true),
  ('sen-me-jackson', 'immigration', 4, 'Wikipedia, citing a July 2026 debate: "I''d abolish it [ICE] altogether," calling ICE a threat to communities; spoke at a July 14 demonstration outside a federal immigration office in Scarborough. Raised from 2 to 4: abolish ICE by name.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Troy_Jackson', false),
  ('gov-me-king', 'housing', 2, 'Maine Morning Star: support towns adding housing, weatherize aging homes, remove permitting red tape, train building trades workers, protect mobile home owners and house those most in need. Supply focused.', 'https://mainemorningstar.com/voter-guides/contests/2026-gubernatorial-democratic-primary/', true),
  ('ny17-conley', 'gnd', 2, 'BallotReady candidate profile: Conley "will invest in the Hudson Valley by prioritizing clean energy - like solar, wind, and geothermal - to create good-paying jobs, lower utility bills." Clean energy investment without a fossil fuel phaseout.', 'https://www.ballotready.org/people/cait-conley', true),
  ('ny17-conley', 'housing', 2, 'Candidate profile: endorses targeted federal funding and tax credits to support affordable housing and infrastructure. Supply and subsidy focused, no tenant protections.', 'https://www.ballotready.org/people/cait-conley', true),
  ('ny17-conley', 'abortion', 2, 'Campaign platform as reported: supports codifying abortion rights in federal law. No Hyde repeal position found.', 'https://riverjournalonline.com/around-town/politics/meet-the-ny-17-democratic-candidates-cait-conley/303786/', true),
  ('ne02-powell', 'housing', 2, 'Campaign priorities page: "Build more high-quality, affordable housing that is attainable for first-time homebuyers and middle-class families." Supply and homebuyer focused.', 'https://deniseforcongress.org/priorities/', true),
  ('ne02-powell', 'gnd', 2, 'Campaign priorities page: "Expand clean energy production to bring down costs in the short term while protecting our environment in the long run." No fossil fuel phaseout commitment.', 'https://deniseforcongress.org/priorities/', true),
  ('mi10-hines', 'gnd', 1, 'Campaign site criticizes the rollback of environmental protections safeguarding Lake St. Clair and the Great Lakes. No clean energy, emissions or fossil fuel policy on the site.', 'https://www.predictionedge.com/elections/profile/christina-hines/', true),
  ('mi10-hines', 'immigration', 1, 'BallotReady profile: would combat the fentanyl crisis "through increased border security, stricter penalties for the sale of fentanyl and other narcotics." Border-security framing with no immigration policy beyond enforcement.', 'https://www.ballotready.org/people/christina-hines', true),
  ('az01-shah', 'abortion', 2, 'Pro-choice legislative record in the Arizona House, including work to protect access to the abortion pill and expand contraception access; campaign says he will "fight for abortion rights." Roe-standard protection, no Hyde repeal position.', 'https://www.predictionedge.com/elections/profile/amish-shah/', true),
  ('az01-shah', 'immigration', 1, 'Campaign supports increased funding and enforcement to secure the border, emphasizing stopping fentanyl trafficking and tougher penalties, rather than expanded legal pathways or asylum protections.', 'https://www.predictionedge.com/elections/profile/amish-shah/', true),
  ('az01-shah', 'gnd', 1, 'Has a pro-environment voting record and positive ratings from climate organizations in the Arizona legislature, but has published no climate or energy plan on his campaign issues page.', 'https://smarter.vote/races/az-01-house-2026/amish-shah/', true),
  ('gov-wi-crowley', 'gnd', 2, 'Campaign plan: invest in solar, energy retrofits and clean infrastructure creating union jobs, building on cutting Milwaukee County emissions nearly 50%. Clean energy investment without a fossil fuel phaseout.', 'https://www.crowleyforwi.com/Plan', true),
  ('gov-wi-crowley', 'housing', 2, 'Campaign platform names housing supply as one of four first-30-days priorities; as county executive he expanded access to affordable housing. Supply and access focused, no tenant protections or social housing commitment.', 'https://www.crowleyforwi.com/Plan', true),
  ('gov-wi-crowley', 'immigration', 2, 'Opposes local law enforcement partnerships with ICE and supports Milwaukee County policies limiting cooperation. State and county scope; no federal pathway position stated.', 'https://www.predictionedge.com/elections/profile/david-crowley/', true),
  ('gov-wi-crowley', 'tax', 1, 'Supports diversifying local revenue away from property taxes, including a sales tax increase, plus tax relief for working families and code reforms rather than blanket cuts. No proposal to raise taxes on high earners or corporations.', 'https://www.predictionedge.com/elections/profile/david-crowley/', true),
  ('gov-nv-ford', 'labor', 3, 'Nevada Independent candidate comparison: Ford says that as governor he would repeal Nevada’s right-to-work law, the state analogue of the PRO Act’s central provision. No sectoral bargaining or $17 wage commitment, so not 4.', 'https://thenevadaindependent.com/article/from-abortion-to-taxes-where-nevadas-2026-governor-candidates-stand-on-the-issues', true),
  ('gov-nv-ford', 'housing', 2, 'Campaign issues page and Nevada Independent: would limit corporate investors buying single family homes, crack down on predatory landlords, ease permitting and use vacant land. Anti-corporate-landlord and supply focused, no public investment or tenant right to counsel.', 'https://www.fordfornevada.com/issues', true),
  ('gov-nv-ford', 'immigration', 2, 'Issued 72 pages of model immigration policies guiding law enforcement, schools and hospitals to resist unpaid ICE cooperation, and has litigated to protect DACA. Protects Dreamers; no broader pathway position.', 'https://www.nvgov2026.org/candidates/ford.html', true),
  ('gov-nv-ford', 'gnd', 1, 'Perfect environmental voting record as a state legislator and a 96% lifetime Nevada Conservation League score, but no comprehensive climate platform released for the governor’s race and no water or mining policy articulated.', 'https://www.nvgov2026.org/candidates/ford.html', true),
  ('gov-nv-ford', 'tax', 1, 'Nevada Independent: opposes resetting property tax values and his team confirmed in August 2026 that he will not raise taxes, period. No revenue proposal targeting high earners or corporations.', 'https://thenevadaindependent.com/article/from-abortion-to-taxes-where-nevadas-2026-governor-candidates-stand-on-the-issues', true),
  ('gov-mi-benson', 'housing', 2, 'Campaign affordability agenda: boost the number of affordable housing units by reducing red tape for builders, alongside public investment in housing. Supply focused, no tenant protections.', 'https://michiganindependent.com/politics/costs-jocelyn-benson-governor-affordability-2026/', true),
  ('gov-mi-benson', 'tax', 1, 'Proposes a $5,000 caregiver tax credit and opposes tax breaks as the primary tool for attracting business, but has no proposal to raise rates on high earners or corporations.', 'https://michiganindependent.com/politics/michigan-governor-candidates-offer-competing-proposals-on-healthcare-and-education/', true),
  ('gov-mi-benson', 'gnd', 1, 'Her energy agenda is a data center moratorium and guardrails requiring companies to pay for the energy they use, framed around costs. No emissions target or clean energy transition plan published.', 'https://www.wlns.com/your-local-election-hq/meet-the-candidates/meet-the-candidates-jocelyn-benson/', true),
  ('oh13-sykes', 'gaza', 0, 'In the 119th Congress she cosponsors H.R.1229, the United States-Israel Defense Partnership Act of 2025, and resolutions standing with Israel, with no ceasefire, arms-conditioning or humanitarian-access measure on her cosponsorship record. Coded from the arms-transfer clause of level 0; the AIPAC-backing clause was not separately verified.', 'https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/1229/cosponsors', true),
  ('oh13-sykes', 'housing', 2, 'Cosponsors H.R.5443, the Fair Housing Improvement Act of 2025, and the Affordable Housing Credit Improvement Act. Anti-discrimination and LIHTC expansion, no tenant protections or social housing.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/emilia-sykes/S001223', true),
  ('oh13-sykes', 'immigration', 3, 'Cosponsors H.R.6397, the Dignity for Detained Immigrants Act, which would end federal contracts with private detention facilities and impose detention standards. Detention-contract element of level 4 without a stated pathway to citizenship, so coded 3.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/emilia-sykes/S001223', true),
  ('oh13-sykes', 'tax', 1, 'Cosponsors H.R.2671, the Tax Fairness for Workers Act, restoring the deduction for union dues and unreimbursed expenses. A worker-side deduction, not a proposal to raise rates on top earners.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/emilia-sykes/S001223', true),
  ('oh13-sykes', 'democracy', 1, 'Cosponsors H.R.14, the John R. Lewis Voting Rights Advancement Act of 2025, the Freedom to Vote Act, and the Supreme Court Ethics, Recusal, and Transparency Act. Voting rights bills plus court ethics; no filibuster or Citizens United position, and ethics is not term limits or expansion.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/emilia-sykes/S001223', true),
  ('tx34-gonzalez', 'gaza', 0, 'In the 119th Congress he cosponsors H.R.1229, the United States-Israel Defense Partnership Act of 2025, and H.Res.521 standing with Israel over Iran, following earlier cosponsorship of the Israel Anti-Boycott Act. No ceasefire or arms-conditioning measure on his record. Coded from the arms-transfer clause of level 0; the AIPAC-backing clause was not separately verified.', 'https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/1229/cosponsors', true),
  ('tx34-gonzalez', 'housing', 2, 'Cosponsors the Rural Housing Regulatory Relief Act and Native American Housing Assistance reauthorization in the 119th Congress, and previously the Affordable Housing Credit Improvement Act and Emergency Rental Assistance. Also cosponsors H.R.1078, the Respect State Housing Laws Act, which limits federal eviction moratoriums.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/vicente-gonzalez/G000581', true),
  ('tx34-gonzalez', 'justice', 2, 'Cosponsored the George Floyd Justice in Policing Act in 2020 but is not on the 2025 reintroduction, H.R.5361. Cannabis-related measures only in the current Congress. Historic support that has lapsed, so below the level 3 that names the George Floyd Act.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/vicente-gonzalez/G000581', true),
  ('tx34-gonzalez', 'tax', 1, 'Cosponsors the Tax Fairness for Workers Act and the Restoring Tax Fairness for States and Localities Act, a SALT deduction cap repeal whose benefits flow largely to high earners. No proposal to raise top rates.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/vicente-gonzalez/G000581', true),
  ('tx34-gonzalez', 'democracy', 1, 'Cosponsors H.R.14, the John R. Lewis Voting Rights Advancement Act of 2025, and the Freedom to Vote Act. Voting rights bills only; no filibuster or Citizens United position.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/vicente-gonzalez/G000581', true),
  ('ia01-bohannan', 'gnd', 2, 'Priorities page frames climate through farm and insurance costs and backs significant investment rather than unfunded mandates; supports expanding wind and solar and farmer-led carbon sequestration. Clean energy expansion without a fossil fuel phaseout.', 'https://bohannanforcongress.com/priorities/', true),
  ('ia01-bohannan', 'housing', 2, 'Campaign focus includes restricting investor purchases of residential property alongside general cost-of-living measures. Anti-investor, no tenant protections or public investment commitment.', 'https://leadershipnowproject.org/candidates/christina-bohannan/', true),
  ('ia01-bohannan', 'tax', 1, 'Supports lower taxes for the middle class while wealthy individuals and large corporations pay a fairer share, plus an expanded child tax credit. Fair-share framing with no specific rate increase or wealth tax proposal.', 'https://www.predictionedge.com/elections/profile/christina-bohannan/', true),
  ('ia01-bohannan', 'immigration', 2, 'Supports bipartisan reform combining enforcement with legalization and workforce adjustments, and criticizes Congress for failing to pass the bipartisan border bill. Legalization component present but no specific pathway named.', 'https://www.predictionedge.com/elections/profile/christina-bohannan/', true),
  ('wi03-cooke', 'immigration', 2, 'WEAU, August 2026: "We need a commonsense immigration policy that includes a secure border and a pathway to citizenship," supports the bipartisan Dignity Act as a first step, argues workers without criminal histories need a legal way to keep contributing. Pathway with enforcement; coded 2.', 'https://www.weau.com/2026/08/16/decision-2026-cooke-van-orden-agree-pocketbook-pressures-split-over-causes-solutions/', false),
  ('wi03-cooke', 'tax', 1, 'Ballotpedia Candidate Connection survey: campaign messages are better wages, more economic opportunity and lower taxes for working families. No proposal to raise rates on high earners or corporations.', 'https://ballotpedia.org/Rebecca_Cooke', true),
  ('pa08-cognetti', 'abortion', 2, 'Guides.vote candidate comparison: "[Abortion] needs to be legal, it needs to be safe," and says it matters to elect leaders who "will protect a woman’s right to choose." Supports the Roe standard; no federal codification or Hyde language found.', 'https://guides.vote/guide/2026-pennsylvania-pa-08-us-house-voters-guide/', true),
  ('pa08-cognetti', 'gnd', 2, 'Guides.vote: called the Inflation Reduction Act and its $369 billion in clean energy investment the "historic investment that we need to prevent the worst effects of climate change," and developed a Climate Action Plan as mayor of Scranton. IRA-style incentives, no fossil fuel phaseout.', 'https://guides.vote/guide/2026-pennsylvania-pa-08-us-house-voters-guide/', true),
  ('pa08-cognetti', 'm4a', 1, 'Guides.vote: would stop health care middlemen denying prescribed care, supports fully funding ACA premium subsidies, and opposes the Medicaid cuts in the 2025 reconciliation bill. Coverage defense within the current system; no public option or single payer position.', 'https://guides.vote/guide/2026-pennsylvania-pa-08-us-house-voters-guide/', true),
  ('pa08-cognetti', 'labor', 2, 'MoveOn endorsement profile: supports making it easier to start or join a union and promoting union-backed jobs, and is endorsed by major labor unions. No PRO Act commitment or minimum wage figure found.', 'https://front.moveon.org/endorsements/candidates/paige-cognetti/', true),
  ('oh09-kaptur', 'gaza', 3, 'Cosponsors H.Res.473 in the 119th Congress calling for urgent delivery and disbursement of humanitarian aid to Gaza. Humanitarian access without an arms-conditioning or blocking measure, so 3 rather than 4.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/marcy-kaptur/K000009', true),
  ('oh09-kaptur', 'tax', 1, 'Cosponsors H.R.2671, the Tax Fairness for Workers Act, restoring the union dues deduction. A worker-side deduction, not a proposal to raise rates on top earners.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/marcy-kaptur/K000009', true),
  ('oh09-kaptur', 'democracy', 1, 'Cosponsors H.R.14, the John R. Lewis Voting Rights Advancement Act of 2025. Voting rights only; no filibuster, Citizens United or court reform position on her 119th Congress record.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/marcy-kaptur/K000009', true),
  ('tx28-cuellar', 'gaza', 0, 'Cosponsors H.R.1229, the United States-Israel Defense Partnership Act of 2025, and H.R.7540, the United States-Israel FUTURES Act of 2026, with no ceasefire, arms-conditioning or humanitarian-access measure on his 119th Congress record. Coded from the arms-transfer clause of level 0; the AIPAC clause was not separately verified.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/henry-cuellar/C001063', true),
  ('tx28-cuellar', 'housing', 2, 'Cosponsors H.R.2840, the Housing Supply Frameworks Act, which supports state and local zoning reform to increase supply. Supply focused, no tenant protections or public investment.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/henry-cuellar/C001063', true),
  ('tx28-cuellar', 'tax', 1, 'Cosponsors the Tax Fairness for Workers Act and the Small Business Tax Fairness and Compliance Simplification Act. No proposal to raise rates on high earners or corporations.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/henry-cuellar/C001063', true),
  ('tx28-cuellar', 'democracy', 1, 'Cosponsors H.R.14, the John R. Lewis Voting Rights Advancement Act of 2025. Voting rights only; no filibuster or Citizens United position.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/henry-cuellar/C001063', true),
  ('sen-nc-cooper', 'immigration', 2, 'As governor he vetoed HB 370, SB 101 and HB 10, bills requiring sheriffs to cooperate with ICE. Opposes mandated local immigration enforcement; no federal pathway position stated in the Senate campaign.', 'https://enlacelatinonc.org/en/Roy-Cooper-launches-Senate-campaign-for-2026/', true),
  ('sen-nc-cooper', 'justice', 1, 'Campaigns on his record as a prosecutor and on a sharp decrease in crime while defending the 2021 court-ordered COVID prison release settlement. General reform framing; no qualified immunity, cash bail or George Floyd Act position.', 'https://battlegroundvote.com/north-carolina/roy-cooper', true),
  ('sen-nc-cooper', 'tax', 2, 'Opposes corporate tax cuts he says come at the expense of the middle class and schools, and vetoed a state budget over income tax cuts that would have limited teacher raises. Opposition to top-end cuts without a proposal to raise rates.', 'https://battlegroundvote.com/north-carolina/roy-cooper', true),
  ('ca22-villegas', 'housing', 3, 'Housing page: "I will fight to end corporate ownership of single-family homes" and "We need an ambitious federal program to build an abundance of affordable and safe housing across the country, creating hundreds of thousands of well-paid union jobs." Public investment at scale; no rent stabilization or tenant right to counsel, so not 4.', 'https://www.villegasforcongress.com/issues/housing', false),
  ('ca22-villegas', 'gnd', 2, 'Environment page: prioritise farmworker health against extreme heat, hold corporate polluters accountable for gas leaks, air pollution and water contamination, and expand national parks and wildlife conservation. Jobs page adds a just transition guaranteeing all energy workers well-paid secure jobs. No fossil fuel phaseout, no end to subsidies or leasing, and the Green New Deal is not named.', 'https://www.villegasforcongress.com/issues/environment', true),
  ('ca22-villegas', 'tax', 4, 'Jobs and the Economy page: "The most effective and fair way to increase government revenue is to tax the top 1% of income earners and wealth holders, and give working families the break we’ve earned." Taxing wealth holders is level 4 in substance, though no wealth tax or billionaire minimum tax bill is named.', 'https://www.villegasforcongress.com/issues/jobs-the-economy', true),
  ('ca22-villegas', 'immigration', 3, 'Immigration page: calls blanket detention and deportation unconstitutional and un-American and commits to "a working system that protects our communities while providing a path to citizenship so our undocumented neighbors, friends and coworkers aren’t forced to live in the shadows," plus returning deported veterans. Pathway for all undocumented; does not commit to defunding or abolishing ICE enforcement or ending detention contracts, so not 4.', 'https://www.villegasforcongress.com/issues/immigration-1', false),
  ('ca22-villegas', 'antitrust', 3, 'Jobs page: "No corporations should be allowed to become large enough to control an entire sector." AI page adds data privacy legislation, AI safety regulation and making large AI companies pay their fair share. Corruption page adds a congressional stock trading and lobbying ban. Breakups and Big Tech regulation without private equity or crypto commitments, so not 4.', 'https://www.villegasforcongress.com/issues/jobs-the-economy', false),
  ('ca22-villegas', 'democracy', 2, 'Fight Political Corruption page: "We must seek every legal avenue available to end Citizens United, and ban corporate PACs," plus congressional term limits and a stock trading and lobbying ban. No position on the filibuster or Supreme Court reform, so below level 3.', 'https://www.villegasforcongress.com/issues/fight-political-corruption', true),
  ('ny17-conley', 'gaza', 1, 'At an April 2026 candidate forum she distanced herself from Senate Democratic efforts to block certain military sales to Israel, while saying she opposes actions by the Netanyahu government and supports the US-Israel alliance. Endorsed by Democratic Majority for Israel. Opposes blocking arms transfers but is not unconditional, so 1 rather than 0.', 'https://www.jta.org/2026/06/23/ny/pro-israel-democrats-battle-to-take-on-vulnerable-republican-rep-mike-lawler', true),
  ('gov-az-hobbs', 'labor', 3, 'Campaign record: launched a first-in-the-nation Heat Stress State Emphasis Plan requiring water, shade and rest for outdoor workers, brokered a labor agreement at TSMC, signed bipartisan wage theft enforcement legislation, doubled apprenticeships and blocked efforts to erode workers’ rights. Endorsed by IAM and Ironworkers Local 75. Substantive pro-labor governing record; the PRO Act and sectoral bargaining are federal and outside her office.', 'https://katiehobbs.org/katie-hobbs-secures-the-endorsement-of-the-iam-union-arizona-state-council/', true),
  ('gov-az-hobbs', 'gnd', 2, 'Arizona Ballot Guide: supports green energy development and says climate change affects every aspect of Arizona governance; her Energy Promise Task Force produced a state strategic energy plan addressing data center demand and utility bills. Clean energy development without a fossil fuel phaseout.', 'https://arizonaballotguide.com/candidates/katie-hobbs', true),
  ('ne02-powell', 'gaza', 2, 'At a candidate forum she called it heartbreaking to watch innocent lives destroyed and said Netanyahu’s right-wing government "has gone way too far," and said she would have hesitated over a State Department bill blocking UNRWA funding, citing concern about stripping humanitarian aid to Gaza. Ceasefire and humanitarian framing without support for conditioning or blocking arms transfers.', 'https://nebraskaexaminer.com/2026/05/09/ne-02-race-dems-sound-similar-on-israel-palestine-but-subtle-differences-exist/', true),
  ('az01-shah', 'gaza', 0, 'His April 2024 Middle East position paper backs continued US aid to Israel with no additional restrictions and supports Israel''s war against Hamas, and Algemeiner reported in July 2026 that he has defended that war. No ceasefire, arms-conditioning or humanitarian-access position found. Coded 0 on the arms-transfer clause only: the AIPAC-backing half of level 0 is affirmatively untrue for him, since AIPAC-funded Bold America spent $1.75M against him. The position paper is from 2024 and may be stale.', 'https://jewishinsider.com/2024/10/amish-shah-david-schweikert-arizona-swing-district-jewish-community/', true),
  ('mi10-hines', 'tax', 2, 'Macomb Defenders candidate questionnaire, her campaign''s own answer: "Lower taxes for middle class, higher taxes for billionaires. Good jobs and fair wages." Raising taxes on billionaires without naming a wealth tax or billionaire minimum tax.', 'https://macombdefenders.com/voters-guide/', true),
  ('mi10-hines', 'abortion', 2, 'Macomb Defenders questionnaire, her campaign''s answer: "Protect Voting Rights. Reproductive Freedom Champion. Freedom for ALL." Endorsed by EMILY''s List. Supports the Roe standard; no codification bill or Hyde repeal named.', 'https://macombdefenders.com/voters-guide/', true),
  ('mi10-hines', 'democracy', 1, 'Macomb Defenders questionnaire: her campaign lists protecting voting rights as a lead priority. No position on the filibuster, Citizens United or court reform, unlike primary rival Greimel who named the John Lewis Act and the Freedom to Vote Act.', 'https://macombdefenders.com/voters-guide/', true),
  ('ne02-powell', 'tax', 1, 'Campaign about page attacks ''massive tax breaks for billionaires like Elon Musk'' and the cost of Trump trade wars. Opposition to top-end tax cuts with no proposal to raise rates on high earners or corporations.', 'https://www.boldpac.com/candidates/denise-powell', true),
  ('nj07-bennett', 'gnd', 2, 'Campaign site: "ready to address the climate crisis by investing in renewable energy, creating jobs, and lowering energy costs in New Jersey." Clean energy investment without a fossil fuel phaseout.', 'https://rebeccabennettforcongress.com/', true),
  ('nj07-bennett', 'labor', 2, 'Endorsed by the Amalgamated Transit Union, SMART-TD and CWA District 1, cited for her commitment to transit workers and infrastructure investment. Union support and pro-worker framing; the PRO Act and a minimum wage figure are not named anywhere on her site.', 'https://rebeccabennettforcongress.com/', true),
  ('nj07-bennett', 'antitrust', 2, 'Campaign has repeatedly attacked Kean over congressional stock trading, fact-checking his unkept blind trust promise and his position that members should be able to sell individual stocks. Implies support for a trading ban; no antitrust or Big Tech position published.', 'https://rebeccabennettforcongress.com/', true),
  ('nj07-bennett', 'tax', 1, 'Criticised Kean''s vote for the 2025 Trump tax legislation and campaigns on affordability. Opposition to that package without a stated proposal to raise rates on high earners.', 'https://rebeccabennettforcongress.com/', true),
  ('sen-ia-turek', 'democracy', 4, 'Platform: pass a constitutional amendment to reverse Citizens United, pass the DISCLOSE Act, ban corporate PAC money, set term limits for members of Congress and Supreme Court justices, and enforce ethics standards on the Court. Citizens United plus Supreme Court term limits meets level 4; no filibuster position stated.', 'https://turek4iowa.com/platform/', true),
  ('sen-ia-turek', 'antitrust', 2, 'Platform: ban members of Congress and their spouses from trading stock, and he has sponsored state legislation capping campaign contributions. Stock trading ban without an antitrust or Big Tech position.', 'https://turek4iowa.com/platform/', false),
  ('pa01-harvie', 'abortion', 2, 'BallotReady: "Abortion is healthcare. I believe that women should be able to make their own reproductive healthcare choices, not the government. I''ll support funding Planned Parenthood." Supports the Roe standard; no codification bill or Hyde repeal named.', 'https://www.ballotready.org/people/robert-harvie', true),
  ('pa01-harvie', 'gnd', 2, 'As county commissioner he championed a County Climate Action Plan, hired a sustainability director and passed resolutions toward 100% renewable energy; campaigns on modernising infrastructure to cut emissions and expand clean energy. Clean energy incentives without a fossil fuel phaseout.', 'https://www.politicspa.com/elections/candidates/bob-harvie', true),
  ('pa01-harvie', 'labor', 2, 'Campaign priorities include a $15 minimum wage and supporting unions. Below the $17 threshold in level 4 and the PRO Act is not named.', 'https://www.inquirer.com/politics/nation/bob-harvie-democrat-bucks-county-commissioner-brian-fitzpatrick-20260329.html', true),
  ('pa01-harvie', 'tax', 2, 'Supports middle-class tax relief while closing loopholes so the ultra-wealthy and large corporations pay more. Top-end loophole closure without a rate increase or wealth tax proposal.', 'https://www.politicspa.com/elections/candidates/bob-harvie', true),
  ('pa01-harvie', 'democracy', 3, 'Would support a constitutional amendment to overturn Citizens United, and would ban members of Congress from trading individual stocks and from becoming lobbyists. Citizens United commitment without a filibuster or Court reform position.', 'https://www.inquirer.com/politics/nation/bob-harvie-democrat-bucks-county-commissioner-brian-fitzpatrick-20260329.html', true),
  ('pa01-harvie', 'justice', 1, 'BallotReady: would increase funding for local law enforcement and expand co-responder programs embedding social workers with police. More police funding paired with a diversion reform; no qualified immunity or decarceration position.', 'https://www.ballotready.org/people/robert-harvie', false),
  ('pa01-harvie', 'antitrust', 2, 'Would ban members of Congress from trading individual stocks and from becoming lobbyists. Stock trading ban without an antitrust or Big Tech position.', 'https://www.ballotready.org/people/robert-harvie', false),
  ('ny12-lasher', 'housing', 4, 'Abundance NY questionnaire: repeal the Faircloth Amendment barring construction of new public housing, major expansion of Section 8 vouchers, expand tax credits and rental assistance, Build More Housing Near Transit Act. Authored New York''s largest housing supply package. Repealing Faircloth is a social housing commitment.', 'https://voterguide.abundanceny.org/questionnaires/micah-lasher-questionnaire', false),
  ('ny12-lasher', 'labor', 3, 'Committed to cosponsor the PRO Act per the CPC PAC endorsement, and campaigns on raising and indexing the federal minimum wage, which he already did at state level. No sectoral bargaining or $17 figure named.', 'https://weareprogressives.org/congressional-progressive-caucus-pac-endorses-micah-lasher-for-ny-12/', true),
  ('ny12-lasher', 'tax', 4, 'Abundance NY questionnaire: repeal Trump''s tax breaks for the rich. City & State: supports taxing wealth and large corporations, proposes a luxury pied-a-terre tax and authored the MEGA Corporations Act requiring multinationals to count global profits for state tax. Taxing wealth by name.', 'https://www.cityandstateny.com/prediction-markets/candidates/micah-lasher', true),
  ('ny12-lasher', 'gnd', 3, 'Supports banning gas in new buildings, economywide cap-and-invest, expanding renewables and restoring clean energy tax credits "to end our reliance on fossil fuels." Fossil fuel phaseout intent without Green New Deal language or a leasing commitment.', 'https://www.cityandstateny.com/prediction-markets/candidates/micah-lasher', true),
  ('ny12-lasher', 'immigration', 4, 'Abundance NY questionnaire lists "abolishing ICE" among the Trump abuses he would stop. Meets the defund-or-abolish-ICE element of level 4.', 'https://voterguide.abundanceny.org/questionnaires/micah-lasher-questionnaire', true),
  ('ny12-lasher', 'antitrust', 2, 'Platform: vote to ban stock trading by members of Congress, demand aggressive oversight of pay-to-play and conflicts of interest, and he introduced state legislation to end corporate spending in campaigns. Stock trading ban without a breakup or Big Tech commitment.', 'https://micahlasher.com/platform-and-policies/', false),
  ('ga13-clark', 'justice', 3, 'BallotReady: would "co-sponsor the George Floyd Justice in Policing Act" and partner with Sen. Ossoff to investigate Georgia''s prison system. Backs police reform without defunding. George Floyd Act by name meets level 3.', 'https://www.ballotready.org/people/jasmine-clark', false),
  ('ga13-clark', 'abortion', 2, 'BallotReady: "In Congress, I will work to codify the right to privacy in medical decisions." Longtime reproductive rights advocate in the Georgia House. Codification commitment without Hyde repeal.', 'https://www.ballotready.org/people/jasmine-clark', true),
  ('ga13-clark', 'gnd', 2, 'Supports climate action and investment in renewable energy; profiles note she does not call for Green New Deal-style measures. Clean energy investment without a fossil fuel phaseout.', 'https://www.predictionedge.com/elections/profile/jasmine-clark/', true),
  ('ga13-clark', 'tax', 2, 'Opposed large regressive income tax cuts and the flat-rate replacement in Georgia, arguing for maintaining revenue for public services rather than cuts that benefit higher earners. Opposition to top-end cuts without a rate increase or wealth tax proposal.', 'https://electionsga.com/candidates/jasmine-clark', true),
  ('ga13-clark', 'immigration', 2, 'Supports protecting immigrant communities and in-state tuition access for immigrant students. Dreamer-focused protections without a broader pathway position.', 'https://electionsga.com/candidates/jasmine-clark', true),
  ('ga13-clark', 'labor', 2, 'BallotReady: will champion investment in apprenticeships including union apprenticeship programs. Pro-union framing without the PRO Act or a wage figure.', 'https://www.ballotready.org/people/jasmine-clark', true),
  ('il07-ford', 'antitrust', 3, 'Voted for Illinois SB 1797, the Digital Assets and Consumer Protection Act, which imposed compliance and consumer-protection rules on crypto firms, drawing $5.0M in opposition spending from the Fairshake crypto super PAC. Crypto regulation in practice; no stock trading ban or Big Tech breakup position published.', 'https://chronicleillinois.com/news/cook-county-news/davis-denounces-attack-ad-by-crypto-pac-on-ford-in-7th-congress-primary/', false),
  ('il07-ford', 'housing', 3, 'WTTW voter guide: will invest more federal funds in affordable housing for seniors and working families; born in Cabrini-Green and has worked on affordable housing access as a state legislator. Public investment commitment without rent stabilization or right to counsel.', 'https://news.wttw.com/elections/voters-guide/2026-primary/lashawn-k-ford', true),
  ('il07-ford', 'democracy', 1, 'WTTW voter guide: running to "defend our democracy" against assaults on voting rights; has worked to enshrine the right to vote in Illinois. Voting rights only, no filibuster or Citizens United position.', 'https://news.wttw.com/elections/voters-guide/2026-primary/lashawn-k-ford', true),
  ('az06-mendoza', 'gaza', 2, 'Endorsed by JStreetPAC, and "has committed to representing J Street''s pro-Israel, pro-peace values in Congress." J Street supports a ceasefire and two-state diplomacy; no statement of her own on conditioning or blocking arms transfers found, so 2.', 'https://jstreetpac.org/candidate/joanna-mendoza/', true),
  ('sen-il-stratton', 'immigration', 4, 'Campaigned on abolishing ICE and repeated it in her March 17 victory speech: "We will fight to abolish ICE." Meets the abolish-ICE element of level 4.', 'https://www.pbs.org/newshour/nation/illinois-lt-gov-juliana-stratton-wins-democratic-primary-for-u-s-senate', false),
  ('sen-il-stratton', 'labor', 4, 'WTTW voter guide: "We need to raise the federal minimum wage to $25 an hour," building on the $15 Illinois wage she helped pass, and calls for a real living wage. Clears the $17 threshold; the PRO Act and sectoral bargaining are not named, so this rests on the wage element and union backing.', 'https://news.wttw.com/elections/voters-guide/2026-primary/juliana-stratton', true),
  ('sen-il-stratton', 'gaza', 1, 'Al Jazeera reports she took money from pro-Israel donors during the primary, while primary rival Robin Kelly criticised her for declining to label the bombardment of Gaza. No ceasefire, conditioning or arms position of her own found. Coded 1: below the ceasefire threshold but not unconditional support.', 'https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/18/pro-israel-groups-see-mixed-record-in-money-fuelled-illinois-primaries', true),
  ('ca11-chan', 'gaza', 4, 'Campaign issues page: "Connie Chan will be an immediate sponsor of the Block the Bombs Act which would prohibit the United States from transferring weapons that have been used by the Israeli military in Gaza," calls for a permanent ceasefire and a major expansion of humanitarian aid, and describes the genocide of the Palestinian people. Pledged a total arms embargo and rejection of AIPAC support in the Track AIPAC questionnaire. Campaigns on blocking offensive arms transfers and refuses AIPAC.', 'https://www.conniechansf.com/issues/global-security', false),
  ('ca11-chan', 'no_corp_pac', 3, 'Track AIPAC questionnaire: rejects corporate PAC money and backs a constitutional amendment to overturn Citizens United. Elect Democratic Women, whose PAC network received AIPAC funding, has spent for her through intermediaries, which she did not solicit. Pledge alongside indirect outside support; no explicit disavowal of super PAC spending found.', 'https://x.com/TrackAIPAC/status/2079552147809607957', true),
  ('ca11-chan', 'democracy', 3, 'Track AIPAC questionnaire: backs a constitutional amendment to overturn Citizens United. No filibuster or Supreme Court reform position found.', 'https://x.com/TrackAIPAC/status/2079552147809607957', true),
  ('ca45-tran', 'gaza', 4, 'Cosponsors H.R.3565, the Block the Bombs Act, limiting transfers of offensive weapons to Israel, and H.J.Res.84 disapproving a proposed foreign military sale, plus H.Res.473 on humanitarian aid to Gaza. Cosponsors bills blocking offensive arms transfers; the AIPAC clause of level 4 was not separately verified.', 'https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/3565/cosponsors', true),
  ('ca45-tran', 'housing', 2, 'Cosponsors H.R.2725, the Affordable Housing Credit Improvement Act of 2025, and Native American housing reauthorisation. LIHTC expansion without tenant protections or public investment.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/derek-tran/T000491', false),
  ('ca45-tran', 'immigration', 2, 'Cosponsors H.R.4456, the Stop ICE from Kidnapping U.S. Citizens Act, H.R.7297, the ICE and CBP Constitutional Accountability Act, and H.R.5387, the Saving the American Dream Act. Enforcement accountability and a Dreamer measure; no broad pathway bill.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/derek-tran/T000491', true),
  ('ca45-tran', 'democracy', 1, 'Cosponsors H.R.14, the John R. Lewis Voting Rights Advancement Act of 2025. Voting rights only.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/derek-tran/T000491', false),
  ('tx18-menefee', 'gaza', 4, 'Cosponsors H.R.3565, the Block the Bombs Act, limiting transfers of offensive weapons to Israel. Cosponsors a bill blocking offensive arms transfers; the AIPAC clause of level 4 was not separately verified.', 'https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/3565/cosponsors', true),
  ('tx18-menefee', 'democracy', 3, 'Cosponsors H.R.3544, the Supreme Court TERM Act establishing term limits, H.R.3513 on Court ethics and recusal, and H.R.14, the John R. Lewis Voting Rights Advancement Act. Court term limits meet the level 4 marker, but no filibuster or Citizens United cosponsorship found, so 3.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/christian-menefee/M001245', true),
  ('tx18-menefee', 'housing', 2, 'Cosponsors H.R.3696, the Fair and Equal Housing Act of 2025, and a resolution on stable housing keeping families together. Anti-discrimination without a public investment or tenant protection bill.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/christian-menefee/M001245', true),
  ('tx18-menefee', 'tax', 1, 'Cosponsors H.R.2671, the Tax Fairness for Workers Act, restoring the union dues deduction. Not a proposal to raise rates on top earners.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/christian-menefee/M001245', false),
  ('tx18-menefee', 'immigration', 2, 'Cosponsors H.R.10040, the No TSA Data for ICE Act. Enforcement data restriction without a pathway bill.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/christian-menefee/M001245', true),
  ('nc01-davis', 'housing', 2, 'Cosponsors H.R.2725, the Affordable Housing Credit Improvement Act, H.R.4957, the Rural Housing Service Reform Act, and shipyard workforce housing. LIHTC and rural supply without tenant protections.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/don-davis/D000230', false),
  ('nc01-davis', 'tax', 1, 'Cosponsors H.R.2671, the Tax Fairness for Workers Act. Not a proposal to raise rates on top earners.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/don-davis/D000230', false),
  ('nc01-davis', 'democracy', 1, 'Cosponsors H.R.14, the John R. Lewis Voting Rights Advancement Act of 2025. Voting rights only.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/don-davis/D000230', false),
  ('sen-nh-pappas', 'housing', 2, 'Cosponsors H.R.2725, the Affordable Housing Credit Improvement Act, H.R.7243, the SPUR Housing Act, and HUD grant authorisation. LIHTC and supply bills without tenant protections.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/chris-pappas/P000614', false),
  ('sen-nh-pappas', 'democracy', 1, 'Cosponsors H.R.14, the John R. Lewis Voting Rights Advancement Act, and H.R.3513, the Supreme Court Ethics, Recusal, and Transparency Act. Voting rights plus Court ethics; no filibuster, Citizens United or term limits position.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/chris-pappas/P000614', false),
  ('sen-il-kelly', 'gaza', 4, 'Cosponsors H.R.3565, the Block the Bombs Act, limiting transfers of offensive weapons to Israel, and criticised her Senate primary rivals for declining to call the Gaza bombardment a genocide. Cosponsors a bill blocking offensive arms transfers; AIPAC clause not separately verified.', 'https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/3565/cosponsors', true),
  ('gov-oh-acton', 'democracy', 0, 'Signal Ohio: supports requiring photo ID to vote in person, a Republican-backed restriction. Backing a voter ID requirement is the opposite of the level 1 voting rights position.', 'https://signalohio.org/amy-acton-ohio-medicaid-voter-id-transgender-athletes-positions-november-election-2026/', true),
  ('gov-oh-acton', 'tax', 1, 'ActOn Lowering Costs agenda: child tax credits of $500 to $1,000 and a refundable credit for lower-income families, with few specifics on funding. Opposes Ramaswamy''s income tax elimination. Credits for working families without a proposal to raise rates on the wealthy.', 'https://www.statenews.org/government-politics/2026-04-06/ohio-governor-race-acton-releases-lots-of-affordability-ideas-but-few-specifics-on-funding-them', true),
  ('gov-oh-acton', 'gnd', 1, 'Has called for restrictions on the data center boom alongside every other candidate for governor. No emissions, clean energy or fossil fuel position published.', 'https://www.statenews.org/government-politics/2026-04-06/ohio-governor-race-acton-releases-lots-of-affordability-ideas-but-few-specifics-on-funding-them', true),
  ('gov-ga-bottoms', 'housing', 3, 'Campaign: crack down on corporate landlords buying up hundreds of properties, add regulations on corporate landlords, and expand and preserve affordable housing units as she did as Atlanta mayor. Public investment plus landlord-side regulation, no rent stabilization or right to counsel.', 'https://www.redandblack.com/athensnews/georgia-governor-candidate-keisha-lance-bottoms-comes-to-athens-on-campaign-trail/article_1cd1a6c2-f9bc-455b-8eaa-2772fbb4e610.html', true),
  ('gov-ga-bottoms', 'abortion', 2, 'Georgia Recorder: pledged to seek to roll back Georgia''s abortion restrictions; branch.vote lists her as supporting abortion access. State-office scope; restoring access rather than federal codification.', 'https://georgiarecorder.com/2026/05/19/former-atlanta-mayor-keisha-lance-bottoms-wins-democratic-nomination-for-georgia-governor/', true),
  ('gov-ga-bottoms', 'tax', 1, 'Pledges income tax cuts, eliminating state income tax for teachers, and targeted relief for veterans and military retirees; no proposal raising taxes on high earners or corporations.', 'https://georgiarecorder.com/2026/05/19/former-atlanta-mayor-keisha-lance-bottoms-wins-democratic-nomination-for-georgia-governor/', true),
  ('gov-ga-bottoms', 'democracy', 1, 'Georgia Recorder: has raised the alarm that the recent Supreme Court voting rights decision could reverse Black political gains, campaigning on protecting voting rights. Voting rights only.', 'https://georgiarecorder.com/2026/05/19/former-atlanta-mayor-keisha-lance-bottoms-wins-democratic-nomination-for-georgia-governor/', true),
  ('ut01-mcadams', 'abortion', 2, 'Has described himself as personally opposed to abortion except for rape, incest or the life of the mother, but supports restoring and codifying the federal right to choose after Dobbs, and held a 100% Planned Parenthood rating in the state Senate. Codify Roe with personal reservations; no Hyde position.', 'https://www.predictionedge.com/elections/profile/ben-mcadams/', true),
  ('ut01-mcadams', 'immigration', 3, 'Supports comprehensive reform combining border security with expanded legal pathways, a permanent DACA solution and pathways to residency or citizenship for undocumented immigrants; has condemned ICE detentions of citizens and removals without due process. Broad pathway with an enforcement component.', 'https://www.predictionedge.com/elections/profile/ben-mcadams/', true),
  ('ut01-mcadams', 'housing', 3, 'Member of the National Housing Crisis Task Force advising governments on using publicly owned real estate to create affordable housing. Public land and investment approach; no rent stabilization or tenant right to counsel.', 'https://utahnewsdispatch.com/2025/11/13/utah-last-democrat-in-congress-ben-mcadams-running-2026/', true),
  ('ca13-gray', 'gaza', 0, 'Cosponsors H.R.1229, the United States-Israel Defense Partnership Act of 2025, with no ceasefire, conditioning or humanitarian measure on his 119th Congress record. Coded from the arms-transfer clause of level 0; AIPAC clause not separately verified.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/adam-gray/G000605', true),
  ('ca13-gray', 'housing', 2, 'Cosponsors H.R.4479 amending the National Housing Act on HUD lending. Narrow supply and finance measure without tenant protections.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/adam-gray/G000605', true),
  ('ca13-gray', 'democracy', 1, 'Cosponsors H.R.14, the John R. Lewis Voting Rights Advancement Act of 2025. Voting rights only.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/adam-gray/G000605', false),
  ('gov-mn-klobuchar', 'labor', 3, 'Cosponsors S.852, the Senate PRO Act of 2025. No sectoral bargaining or $17 wage cosponsorship found.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/amy-klobuchar/K000367', false),
  ('gov-mn-klobuchar', 'housing', 3, 'Cosponsors S.1515, the Affordable Housing Credit Improvement Act, S.2827, the Fair Housing Improvement Act, and S.310, the Build Housing with Care Act. LIHTC expansion plus anti-discrimination and public investment in supportive housing; no rent stabilization.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/amy-klobuchar/K000367', true),
  ('gov-mn-klobuchar', 'democracy', 1, 'Cosponsors S.2523, the John R. Lewis Voting Rights Advancement Act, and S.1814 and S.5121 on Supreme Court ethics. Voting rights plus Court ethics; no filibuster, Citizens United or term limits cosponsorship.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/amy-klobuchar/K000367', false),
  ('gov-mn-klobuchar', 'tax', 2, 'Cosponsors S.2763, the Keep Billionaires Out of Social Security Act, and S.1286, the Tax Fairness for Workers Act. Raises payroll contributions on the highest earners without a wealth tax or top-rate proposal.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/amy-klobuchar/K000367', true),
  ('gov-ia-sand', 'abortion', 2, 'Has pledged to veto any further restrictions on abortion access and to protect contraception, IVF and surrogacy; criticised the state pausing emergency contraception payments for assault survivors. Iowa has a six-week ban; protects the existing standard without a proposal to restore broader access.', 'https://iowastartingline.com/news/elections/iowa-governor-rob-sand-zach-lahn/', true),
  ('gov-ia-sand', 'immigration', 2, 'Questions the fairness of deporting immigrants who work, follow the rules and pay taxes, and favours limiting state participation in federal immigration enforcement. State-office scope; no pathway position stated.', 'https://iowastartingline.com/news/elections/iowa-governor-rob-sand-zach-lahn/', true),
  ('gov-ia-sand', 'gnd', 1, 'Healthier Iowa for All agenda addresses water quality and cancer rates; profiles note he has not published detailed climate or energy proposals. Environmental framing without clean energy or emissions policy.', 'https://www.predictionedge.com/elections/profile/rob-sand/', true),
  ('sen-ga-ossoff', 'labor', 3, 'Cosponsors S.852, the Senate PRO Act of 2025. No sectoral bargaining or $17 wage cosponsorship found.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/jon-ossoff/O000174', false),
  ('sen-ga-ossoff', 'justice', 1, '119th Congress cosponsorships are prison oversight measures: the Federal Prisons Accountability Act, Prison Staff Safety Enhancement Act and a contraband bill, reflecting his Georgia prison investigations. Oversight without qualified immunity, bail or sentencing reform bills.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/jon-ossoff/O000174', true),
  ('sen-ga-ossoff', 'housing', 1, 'Cosponsors S.1415, the Housing Unhoused Disabled Veterans Act. Narrow veterans measure; no LIHTC, supply or tenant protection bill on his 119th Congress record.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/jon-ossoff/O000174', true),
  ('gov-ca-becerra', 'housing', 2, 'CalMatters: says California must build more housing by cutting permitting times and easing access to affordable housing funds, but declines to name a target; proposes state down-payment assistance for renters. Supply and homebuyer focused.', 'https://calmatters.org/politics/2026/08/california-governor-becerra-profile-promises/', true),
  ('gov-ca-becerra', 'gnd', 1, 'CalMatters: is open to revising California''s climate goals to keep fuel affordable, and on keeping the gas-car phaseout mandate says "it depends." Frames grid resilience as public investment but hedges on existing state climate rules.', 'https://calmatters.org/california-voter-guide-2026/governor/', true),
  ('gov-ca-becerra', 'labor', 1, 'Pledges to defend decent wages that keep pace with basic costs. No stated position on collective bargaining, the PRO Act or a wage figure.', 'https://timesofsandiego.com/politics/2026/05/29/xavier-becerra-california-governor-campaign/', true),
  ('gov-fl-jolly', 'abortion', 2, 'Supports codifying the Roe-Casey standard and would introduce state legislation protecting abortion rights up to viability with medical exceptions, while endorsing parental involvement for minors with abuse exceptions. Reversed from his position as a Republican congressman who said life begins at conception.', 'https://www.predictionedge.com/elections/profile/david-jolly/', true),
  ('gov-fl-jolly', 'immigration', 3, 'Favours streamlined pathways to legal status and more open access for people seeking to contribute; would not require enforcement of 287(g) ICE agreements at the state level and suggested suspending them pending due process review. Broad pathway language with enforcement limits.', 'https://www.predictionedge.com/elections/profile/david-jolly/', true),
  ('gov-fl-jolly', 'gnd', 2, 'Platform: accept climate science, invest in climate resilience and clean water, protect beaches and parks, adopt a sustainability agenda; profiles note no fossil fuel phaseout. Resilience and clean energy investment without a phaseout.', 'https://smarter.vote/races/fl-governor-2026/david-jolly/', true),
  ('gov-fl-jolly', 'housing', 2, 'Campaign focuses on homeowner insurance reform and lowering housing costs, with investment in housing framed as improving lives. Cost and insurance focused, no tenant protections or public housing commitment.', 'https://davidjolly.com/about-david/', true),
  ('pa03-rabb', 'gaza', 4, 'Platform: "The genocide in Gaza must end," immediate and permanent ceasefire, Palestinian right of return under international law, and stop funding human rights violations. Supports a complete embargo on arms sales to Israel; endorsed by Track AIPAC, PAL PAC and Jewish Voice for Peace. Campaigns on blocking arms transfers and refuses AIPAC.', 'https://www.chrisrabb.com/platform', false),
  ('pa03-rabb', 'tax', 3, 'Authored Pennsylvania House Bill 1773, the Fair Share Tax Plan, lowering taxes on wages while substantially raising them on passive income such as dividends, rents and royalties. Capital income reform at state level; no federal wealth tax by name found.', 'https://www.cityandstatepa.com/prediction-markets/candidates/chris-rabb', true),
  ('pa03-rabb', 'immigration', 4, 'Sponsored legislation to make Pennsylvania a sanctuary commonwealth barring local agencies from enforcing federal immigration law; DSA, which endorsed him, describes his platform as including abolishing ICE. Pathway for all plus abolish-ICE alignment.', 'https://www.cityandstatepa.com/prediction-markets/candidates/chris-rabb', true),
  ('pa03-rabb', 'abortion', 2, 'Describes abortion as health care and co-sponsored Pennsylvania legislation protecting access to reproductive health services. Supports the Roe standard; no federal Hyde repeal position found.', 'https://www.cityandstatepa.com/prediction-markets/candidates/chris-rabb', true),
  ('gov-ny-hochul', 'gnd', 1, 'New York Focus, May 2026: she convinced a skeptical legislature to roll back the centerpiece of the Climate Leadership and Community Protection Act in the state budget, while pressing to expand offshore wind. Rolling back the state''s landmark climate law outweighs the wind push.', 'https://nysfocus.com/2026/05/27/clcpa-climate-change-rollbacks-hochul-new-york-emissions', true),
  ('gov-ny-hochul', 'tax', 2, 'City & State: supports middle-class tax cuts, inflation refund checks and an expanded child tax credit while maintaining or extending higher rates on top earners rather than broad corporate cuts. Keeps top-end rates without a wealth tax proposal.', 'https://www.cityandstateny.com/prediction-markets/candidates/kathy-hochul', true),
  ('gov-ny-hochul', 'immigration', 2, '2026 State of the State: backed legislation making it easier to sue federal immigration officers who violate New Yorkers'' constitutional rights, saying protecting New Yorkers means standing up to ICE agents who abuse their power. Enforcement accountability at state level; no pathway position.', 'https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/york-hochul-moves-thread-needle-221928155.html', true),
  ('gov-ny-hochul', 'labor', 2, 'Championed a minimum wage increase in 2025 and frames offshore wind expansion around blue-collar construction jobs. Wage and jobs framing; the PRO Act is federal and no sectoral bargaining position exists.', 'https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/hochul-agenda-blends-trump-fighting-105500029.html', true),
  ('gov-me-bennett', 'm4a', 0, 'Voted against expanding MaineCare and spent years opposing the Affordable Care Act per the Maine Democratic Party and Maine Newsroom; his 2026 plan is a medical debt relief program and MaineCare transparency rather than coverage expansion. Defends the private insurance status quo.', 'https://www.newscentermaine.com/article/news/local/independent-candidate-for-maine-governor-rick-bennett-offers-health-care-affordability-plan/97-9f4793b6-41d5-40e0-aee9-01d14e88d103', true),
  ('gov-me-bennett', 'abortion', 2, 'Says he supports reproductive rights and would not roll back any of the abortion access laws passed since 2019, citing a 92% Planned Parenthood rating for 2025, after being aggressively anti-abortion until 2025. Protects the existing standard; recent reversal.', 'https://www.newscentermaine.com/article/news/local/independent-candidate-for-maine-governor-rick-bennett-offers-health-care-affordability-plan/97-9f4793b6-41d5-40e0-aee9-01d14e88d103', true),
  ('gov-me-bennett', 'housing', 2, 'Press Herald: state down-payment support for first-time buyers, a shared-appreciation mortgage assistance program, incentives for factory-built housing, expanded repair grants and a permitting audit. Homebuyer and supply focused.', 'https://www.pressherald.com/2026/07/01/heres-where-maines-candidates-for-governor-stand-on-key-issues/', true),
  ('gov-me-bennett', 'tax', 1, 'Vision page: eliminate unfair tax exemptions, targeted relief for those who need it most, protect older Mainers from being taxed out of their homes; says Maine taxes are pretty darn high. No proposal to raise rates on the wealthy.', 'https://bennettforgovernor.com/vision', true),
  ('gov-me-pingree', 'abortion', 2, 'Accomplishments page: introduced legislation early in her career to ensure reproductive access and defend abortion as a human right; protected essential women''s health services as HHS committee chair. Protects and defends access; state scope.', 'https://hannahforgovernor.com/accomplishments/', true),
  ('gov-me-pingree', 'labor', 2, 'NewsCenter Maine: says she would seek better relations with labor unions than Governor Mills has had. Pro-union framing without a wage figure or bargaining commitment; the PRO Act is federal.', 'https://www.newscentermaine.com/article/news/politics/elections/candidates/hannah-pingree-campaign-maine-governor-public-service-experience/97-31719b97-3534-4b1c-aced-70476b8d97eb', true),
  ('me02-dunlap', 'labor', 3, 'BallotReady, his own words: "I am 100% pro-labor... fighting for workers'' rights through legislation like the PRO Act." Pledged PRO Act support at the Maine AFL-CIO COPE convention and is endorsed by the Maine AFL-CIO. No sectoral bargaining or $17 wage figure.', 'https://www.ballotready.org/people/matthew-g-dunlap', false),
  ('me02-dunlap', 'democracy', 2, 'Maine Public questionnaire: as Secretary of State he got Trump''s voter fraud commission disbanded, and would support legislation, investigations and impeachment if the executive ignores the courts. Our Revolution cites voting rights as a core commitment. Voting rights defence plus institutional accountability; no Citizens United or filibuster position.', 'https://www.mainepublic.org/politics/2026-04-19/your-vote-2026-profile-matt-dunlap-democrat-for-2nd-district', true),
  ('il09-biss', 'immigration', 4, 'WTTW questionnaire, his own words: "abolishing ICE, fixing our outdated visa system, honoring our promises to DREAMers... creates a real path to citizenship, respects asylum seekers, end Trump''s use of foreign prisons, and bans mass raids." Pathway for all plus abolish ICE.', 'https://news.wttw.com/elections/voters-guide/2026-primary/daniel-biss', false),
  ('il09-biss', 'housing', 3, 'WTTW questionnaire: fight to increase investment in housing that all can afford, spur development near transit, end corporate price gouging on housing; updated Evanston''s zoning code as mayor. Public investment plus anti-gouging; no rent stabilization or right to counsel named.', 'https://news.wttw.com/elections/voters-guide/2026-primary/daniel-biss', false),
  ('il09-biss', 'antitrust', 3, 'WTTW questionnaire: names corporate consolidation across food, health care, technology and consumer goods as the root cause of the affordability crisis, calls to break up corporate monopolies, and will ban stock trading by members of Congress. Antitrust enforcement and breakups; no private equity or crypto regulation named.', 'https://news.wttw.com/elections/voters-guide/2026-primary/daniel-biss', false),
  ('il09-biss', 'democracy', 3, 'WTTW questionnaire: ban stock trading by members of Congress, pass the Government by the People Act, end gerrymandering and stop voter suppression; says big money in politics is at the heart of almost every problem. Small-donor reform and voting rights without an explicit Citizens United amendment or filibuster position; coded 3 on the strength of the package.', 'https://news.wttw.com/elections/voters-guide/2026-primary/daniel-biss', true),
  ('il07-ford', 'immigration', 3, 'WTTW questionnaire: "a path to citizenship for longtime residents, Dreamers, and essential workers, expanded legal work visas, faster and fairer asylum processing, and smart border management that focuses on real threats." Broad pathway; no ICE abolition or detention position.', 'https://news.wttw.com/elections/voters-guide/2026-primary/lashawn-k-ford', false),
  ('il07-ford', 'tax', 1, 'WTTW questionnaire: reduce the tax burden on working families and small businesses, close corporate loopholes, expand the Child Tax Credit; criticises corporate tax breaks. Loophole closure and relief framing with no proposal to raise rates on the wealthy.', 'https://news.wttw.com/elections/voters-guide/2026-primary/lashawn-k-ford', false),
  ('il07-ford', 'labor', 2, 'WTTW questionnaire: will focus on union jobs, apprenticeships and local hiring in federal investment. Pro-union framing without the PRO Act or a wage figure.', 'https://news.wttw.com/elections/voters-guide/2026-primary/lashawn-k-ford', true),
  ('il07-ford', 'gaza', 1, 'WTTW questionnaire foreign policy answer discusses alliances, NATO, defense spending oversight and diplomacy, and never mentions Israel, Gaza or arms transfers. No ceasefire or conditioning position; coded 1 as the floor for a candidate with no stated position rather than left blank, provisional.', 'https://news.wttw.com/elections/voters-guide/2026-primary/lashawn-k-ford', true),
  ('sen-ia-turek', 'labor', 3, 'Platform: "Pass the PRO Act to strengthen our unions and protect collective bargaining," raise the minimum wage and tie raises to inflation, end 14C subminimum wage certificates; sponsored state bills on minimum wage and the right to organize. PRO Act by name; no $17 figure or sectoral bargaining.', 'https://turek4iowa.com/platform/', false),
  ('sen-ia-turek', 'housing', 3, 'Platform: ban Wall Street private equity firms from purchasing single family homes and farmland, simplify permitting for affordable housing; sponsored state bills cutting taxes for first-time buyers and limiting private equity home purchases. Private equity ban plus supply; no rent stabilization or public housing commitment.', 'https://turek4iowa.com/platform/', true),
  ('sen-ia-turek', 'abortion', 2, 'Platform: "Make Roe v. Wade the law of the land again and protect access to contraception and IVF"; wrote and sponsored legislation to repeal Iowa''s near-total abortion ban. Codify Roe; no Hyde repeal.', 'https://turek4iowa.com/platform/', false),
  ('sen-ia-turek', 'tax', 1, 'Platform: cut taxes for the middle class and working families, close loopholes for billionaires and big corporations, ensure billionaires pay their fair share into Social Security. Loophole closure and payroll contribution; no rate increase or wealth tax proposal.', 'https://turek4iowa.com/platform/', true),
  ('sen-ia-turek', 'immigration', 2, 'Platform: bipartisan legislation that strengthens the border and simplifies an earned pathway to citizenship, deport those who commit crimes, stop fentanyl, and regulation and accountability for ICE agents. Pathway with enforcement-first framing.', 'https://turek4iowa.com/platform/', false),
  ('sen-ia-turek', 'gnd', 1, 'Platform frames the environment through Iowa''s water quality and cancer crisis: fund water quality sensors and crack down on chemical polluters. No clean energy, emissions or fossil fuel position.', 'https://turek4iowa.com/platform/', true),
  ('ca11-chan', 'labor', 3, 'Ballotpedia platform text, her own words: "Connie will cosponsor the Richard L. Trumka Protecting the Right to Organize (PRO) Act," plus strengthening OSHA; sole endorsement of the California Federation of Labor Unions and National Nurses United. PRO Act by name; no sectoral bargaining or $17 figure.', 'https://ballotpedia.org/Connie_Chan', false),
  ('ca11-chan', 'immigration', 4, 'Ballotpedia platform text: pathway to citizenship, reaffirm birthright citizenship, protect San Francisco as a sanctuary city, end the raids, full accountability for officials who violated due process, and "an end to the inhuman abuses and discriminatory practices of ICE and CBP." Pathway for all plus ending ICE enforcement abuses; stops short of abolish, coded 4 on the combination, provisional.', 'https://ballotpedia.org/Connie_Chan', true),
  ('ca11-chan', 'tax', 3, 'Mission Local kickoff coverage describes her as a "billionaire-taxer"; as supervisor she backed San Francisco business tax measures on large companies. Higher taxes on the wealthy and large corporations without a federal wealth tax or billionaire minimum tax named.', 'https://www.conniechansf.com/news/connie-chan-calfed-endorsement', true),
  ('tx18-menefee', 'antitrust', 2, 'Cosponsor of H.R.5106, the Restore Trust in Congress Act, barring members and their families from owning or trading stocks as of 2026-03-09. Stock trading ban meets level 2; no breakup or Big Tech bill found.', 'https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/5106/cosponsors', false),
  ('sen-nh-pappas', 'antitrust', 2, 'Cosponsor of H.R.5106, the Restore Trust in Congress Act, barring members and their families from owning or trading stocks as of 2025-10-28. Stock trading ban meets level 2; no breakup or Big Tech bill found.', 'https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/5106/cosponsors', false),
  ('ca45-tran', 'antitrust', 2, 'Original cosponsor of H.R.7852, banning member stock trading with a lifetime lobbying ban (2026-03-05). Stock trading ban meets level 2; no breakup or Big Tech bill found.', 'https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/7852/cosponsors', false),
  ('oh13-sykes', 'justice', 2, 'Cosponsor of H.R.5068, the MORE Act, decriminalizing cannabis federally as of 2026-02-04. Cannabis legalisation meets level 2; no qualified immunity or George Floyd Act cosponsorship in the 119th Congress found.', 'https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/5068/cosponsors', false),
  ('tx37-casar', 'democracy', 3, 'Original cosponsor of H.R.3544, the Supreme Court TERM Act establishing 18-year term limits (2025-05-21). Court term limits meet the level 4 marker; no filibuster or Citizens United cosponsorship found, so 3.', 'https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/3544/cosponsors', false),
  ('sen-mn-flanagan', 'gnd', 3, 'Supports 100% carbon-free electricity by 2040, expanding wind and solar, investment in green hydrogen and green steel, and opposes rollbacks of federal clean energy investment. A carbon-free electricity target with union jobs; no explicit end to fossil subsidies or leasing, no Green New Deal by name.', 'https://www.predictionedge.com/elections/profile/peggy-flanagan/', true),
  ('sen-mn-flanagan', 'justice', 1, 'BallotReady: supports funding local police departments for training and community safety, plus re-entry programs to reduce recidivism. Police funding paired with re-entry investment; no qualified immunity, bail or sentencing reform position.', 'https://www.ballotready.org/people/peggy-flanagan-9d6742e7-0fc7-4943-8a25-a9737d2ba80c', true),
  ('sen-mn-flanagan', 'democracy', 2, 'Campaign priorities: restrict corporate and dark money, require donor disclosure, strengthen voting rights, improve public ethics. Voting rights plus disclosure and dark money limits; no Citizens United amendment, filibuster or Court reform position stated.', 'https://mamdanimovement.com/blogs/mamdani-movement/peggy-flanagan-for-u-s-senate-minnesota-2026-campaign-guide', true),
  ('sen-mn-flanagan', 'housing', 2, 'Campaign priorities list stable housing among core commitments alongside child care and wages, without a specific supply, tenant or public housing mechanism.', 'https://mamdanimovement.com/blogs/mamdani-movement/peggy-flanagan-for-u-s-senate-minnesota-2026-campaign-guide', true),
  ('sen-ne-osborn', 'm4a', 4, 'NBC News, September 1, 2026 debate: Ricketts attacked Osborn over his support for "Medicare for All," and Osborn said he would have voted against the 2025 reconciliation bill. Supports Medicare for All by name, as characterised by his opponent on the debate stage and not disputed.', 'https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-election/gop-sen-pete-ricketts-independent-dan-osborn-clash-fiery-nebraska-sena-rcna595645', true),
  ('sen-ne-osborn', 'democracy', 2, 'The Nation: campaigns against billionaire-bought politics and the corruption of both parties by wealthy donors; opposes the influence of PAC and dark money. Anti-big-money framing without a specific Citizens United amendment, filibuster or Court position.', 'https://www.thenation.com/article/politics/dan-osborn-interview-senate-race-2026/', true),
  ('sen-oh-brown', 'abortion', 2, 'Guides.vote: supports abortion access for all women, voted in 2022 to prohibit government restrictions on abortion access (the Women''s Health Protection Act), voted against a 20-week ban in 2018, and backed Ohio''s 2023 constitutional amendment. Codify Roe; no Hyde repeal vote or cosponsorship cited.', 'https://guides.vote/guide/2026-ohio-senate-voters-guide/', true),
  ('sen-oh-brown', 'gnd', 2, 'Guides.vote: voted for the $369 billion in IRA clean energy tax credits and said in 2021 it was time to tackle climate change, but in 2024 opposed the EPA''s tightened greenhouse gas rule for coal plants as unrealistic and job-killing. IRA-style incentives with resistance to a fossil phaseout.', 'https://guides.vote/guide/2026-ohio-senate-voters-guide/', true),
  ('wi03-cooke', 'justice', 1, 'At a July 2026 La Crosse forum she said she does not support defunding the police; the Van Orden campaign says she called for defunding law enforcement in 2023. Current position is against defunding with no stated reform commitments; generic.', 'https://www.wispolitics.com/2026/van-orden-campaign-flip-flop-cooke-scrambles-to-rewrite-her-record-after-years-of-extreme-positions/', true),
  ('wi03-cooke', 'gnd', 2, 'Endorsed by the NRDC Action Fund and the League of Conservation Voters; campaigns on rural and working-class economics without a published climate plan. Environmental endorsements without a phaseout or Green New Deal commitment; coded 2 on the strength of the endorsements, provisional.', 'https://www.predictionedge.com/elections/profile/rebecca-cooke/', true),
  ('wi03-cooke', 'gaza', 2, 'Endorsed by JStreetPAC, which backs a ceasefire and two-state diplomacy. No statement of her own on conditioning or blocking arms transfers found. Coded 2 on the J Street alignment, provisional.', 'https://www.predictionedge.com/elections/profile/rebecca-cooke/', true),
  ('ny07-valdez', 'tax', 3, 'City & State profile, sourced to her site: supports taxing the wealthy to fund social programs and public ownership, a federal jobs guarantee and the Green New Deal; in the Assembly she "fought to tax the rich." No wealth tax or billionaire minimum tax named in her own platform text; the national DSA agenda she runs on includes one.', 'https://www.cityandstateny.com/prediction-markets/candidates/claire-valdez', true),
  ('ny07-valdez', 'antitrust', 2, 'Issues page: "End the unchecked corporate dominance that has proliferated in our country for too long," plus opt-in consent requirements for generative AI and a data center moratorium. Anti-corporate framing and tech regulation without a stock trading ban or breakup commitment named.', 'https://clairevaldezforcongress.com/issues', true),
  ('ny07-valdez', 'abortion', 2, 'Issues page lists "Guaranteed Reproductive Justice" as a platform plank and includes contraception coverage under Medicare for All. The plank text was not retrievable; coded 2 pending the full memo.', 'https://clairevaldezforcongress.com/issues', true),
  ('sen-mi-el-sayed', 'democracy', 3, 'Final debate: "the biggest risks to our democracy are the filibuster, it''s anti-democratic in the Senate, and money in politics." Ending the filibuster plus money out of politics; no Supreme Court term limits position found.', 'https://abdulforsenate.com/2026/07/new-at-final-debate-dr-abdul-el-sayed-proves-hes-ready-for-november/', false),
  ('sen-mi-el-sayed', 'antitrust', 3, 'Hotline ad: "I want aggressive antitrust enforcement and to hold Wall Street accountable." Antitrust enforcement by name; no stock trading ban, private equity or crypto position retrieved.', 'https://abdulforsenate.com/2026/07/new-ad-1-844-abdul-4-u/', false),
  ('sen-mi-el-sayed', 'housing', 3, 'Hotline ad: "I believe you deserve a home... we need a building boom... massively invest in building new housing in communities across the state, and to stand up against all of those unfair regulations." Public investment in supply; no rent stabilization or right to counsel.', 'https://abdulforsenate.com/2026/07/new-ad-1-844-abdul-4-u/', false),
  ('sen-tx-talarico', 'immigration', 2, 'Factually summary of his platform: preserve orderly asylum processing at the southern border, deploy detection technology at ports of entry for fentanyl. Border-management framing; no pathway to citizenship statement retrieved.', 'https://factually.co/fact-checks/politics/james-talarico-policies-15bbe1', true),
  ('ny10-lander', 'tax', 4, 'Jim Owles questionnaire, his own words: supports "a wealth tax." Wealth tax by name.', 'https://jimowles.org/news/candidate-answers-to-joldc-brad-lander-for-us-congress-ny-10-2026', false),
  ('ny10-lander', 'antitrust', 2, 'Jim Owles questionnaire: attacks Goldman for making millions trading stocks in Congress before proposing a ban; supports banning member stock trading. Stock trading ban; no breakup position retrieved.', 'https://jimowles.org/news/candidate-answers-to-joldc-brad-lander-for-us-congress-ny-10-2026', true),
  ('mi13-mckinney', 'justice', 3, 'Daily Caller and NewsNation: campaigned on reforming the criminal justice system by ending cash bail and changing sentencing guidelines; co-introduced a state bill barring police from tampering with body-camera evidence. Bail and sentencing reform; George Floyd Act and qualified immunity not named.', 'https://dailycaller.com/2026/08/05/michigan-13th-district-primary-mckinney-shri-thanedar/', true),
  ('mi13-mckinney', 'tax', 3, 'NewsNation, citing his campaign site: aims to tax billionaires and corporations. Billionaire and corporate taxation without a wealth tax by name.', 'https://www.newsnationnow.com/politics/2026-midterm-elections/democratic-socialists-2026-elections/', true),
  ('mi13-mckinney', 'abortion', 3, 'NewsNation, citing his site: supports reproductive freedom as an economic and racial justice issue; his Medicare for All plan explicitly covers abortion care, which would end Hyde-style exclusions. Codification plus federal coverage of abortion.', 'https://www.donavanforcongress.com/priorities', true),
  ('sen-me-jackson', 'gaza', 4, 'JTA, July 2026, his own words: "Anybody with eyes and a heart knows the Israeli government is committing genocide in Gaza"; said he would never vote for U.S. military aid to Israel and pledged to reject AIPAC money. Total aid cutoff; refuses AIPAC.', 'https://www.jta.org/2026/07/24/politics/maine-democratic-senate-nominee-in-waiting-troy-jackson-raises-eyebrows-in-the-jewish-community', false),
  ('sen-nc-cooper', 'gaza', 1, 'North State Journal, August 2026: his progressive joint-fundraising partners are vocal on Israel and Gaza, "but Cooper has remained silent." Documented silence from a Senate nominee in a race that could decide control; coded 1 as a provisional floor, the same treatment as Ford.', 'https://nsjonline.com/article/2026/08/cooper-joint-fundraising-with-progressive-senators-tops-726k/', true),
  ('sen-ma-markey', 'housing', 4, 'Cosponsors S.1477, the Housing for All Act of 2025, S.934, the American Housing and Economic Mobility Act, and S.5284, the Green New Deal for Public Housing Act. Social housing investment at scale; tenant right to counsel not found by name.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/edward-markey/M000133', true),
  ('sen-ma-markey', 'immigration', 4, 'Sponsors S.3779, the ICE Out of Our Faces Act, and cosponsors S.2350, the Protect DREAMer Confidentiality Act, and S.4411, the Investing in the American Dream Act, plus a joint resolution disapproving an immigration rule. Direct restriction of ICE enforcement plus Dreamer measures; pathway-for-all bill not found in the 119th.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/edward-markey/M000133', true),
  ('sen-ma-markey', 'justice', 4, 'Cosponsors S.1913, the Ending Qualified Immunity Act, S.3625, the Qualified Immunity Abolition Act, S.3959, the Smarter Sentencing Act, and S.5022, the Cannabis Administration and Opportunity Act. Qualified immunity abolition plus sentencing and cannabis reform.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/edward-markey/M000133', false),
  ('sen-ma-markey', 'labor', 3, 'Cosponsors S.852, the Senate PRO Act of 2025, and S.1310, the No Tax Breaks for Union Busting Act. PRO Act by name; no $17 wage bill or sectoral bargaining found.', 'https://www.congress.gov/member/edward-markey/M000133', false)
on conflict (candidate_id, issue_id) do update set score = excluded.score, evidence = excluded.evidence, source_url = excluded.source_url, provisional = excluded.provisional;

